window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b077-60d48385d38e03a2.json"]={sha256:"60d48385d38e03a28897beb89f2737f5d5761635c90df39e7978ff18a31c50b9",value:{"id":"b077","title":"既有建築基礎隔震改造","titleEn":"Base-isolation retrofit of existing buildings","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從鹽湖城市郡大樓、舊金山市政府與猶他州議會大廈的隔震改造出發，計算隔震後的週期、位移與扭轉放大，設計鉛心橡膠支承與後拉預力托換梁，再處理切柱頂升的荷載轉移、施工期間的地震風險、原型與出廠試驗、強震監測，最後談性質變化的上下限分析、隔震縫維護與交接。","summaryEn":"Starting from the isolation retrofits of the Salt Lake City and County Building, San Francisco City Hall and the Utah State Capitol, compute isolated period, displacement and torsional amplification, design lead-rubber bearings and post-tensioned transfer girders, then handle load transfer by cutting and jacking, earthquake risk during construction, prototype and production tests and strong-motion monitoring, and finally upper- and lower-bound property analysis, moat maintenance and handover.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-seismic-precast-fire","subcategoryTitle":"建築耐震、預鑄與防火","subcategoryTitleEn":"Building seismic, precast and fire safety","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-seismic-precast-fire","learningTags":["structures","st-seismic-precast-fire","bearing"],"architectureFamily":"bearing","architectureNodes":[["上部既有結構","Existing superstructure"],["托換梁與隔震面樓板","Transfer girders and isolation diaphragm"],["鉛心橡膠隔震器","Lead-rubber isolators"],["基礎與隔震縫擋土牆","Foundation and moat wall"],["切柱頂升與臨時支撐","Cutting, jacking and shoring"],["強震監測與維護紀錄","Strong-motion monitoring and maintenance records"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[4,1],[2,5],[0,5]],"diagram":{"type":"bearing","labels":["上部既有結構","托換梁與隔震面樓板","鉛心橡膠隔震器","基礎與隔震縫擋土牆","切柱頂升與臨時支撐"],"labelsEn":["Existing superstructure","Transfer girders and isolation diaphragm","Lead-rubber isolators","Foundation and moat wall","Cutting, jacking and shoring"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：某歷史建築重 W = 216,000 kN，以 54 個鉛心橡膠支承隔震。單一支承：鉛心 150 mm、降伏應力 10 MPa，Q_d ≈ 177 kN；直徑 900 mm、橡膠總厚 200 mm、G = 0.4 MPa，K_d ≈ 1,237 kN/m。設計位移 D = 0.40 m 時 F ≈ 672 kN，K_eff ≈ 1,679 kN/m，β_eff ≈ 16%。系統 K ≈ 90,650 kN/m，T = 2π√(W/(g·K)) ≈ 3.1 s；以 S_D1 = 0.7、B = 1.35，D = g·S_D1·T/(4π²·B) ≈ 9.81×0.7×3.1/(39.48×1.35) ≈ 0.40 m，與假設一致；基底剪力係數約 0.17，約為固定基底的六分之一。平面 60 m × 30 m、偏心 3 m 時角落總位移約 0.50 m，隔震縫取 0.55 m 以上。若採用上限性質（Q_d×1.3、K_d×1.1），單一支承力增為約 774 kN，上部結構設計力增加約 15%；若隔震縫被縮減到 0.30 m，撞擊動能約 3.2 MJ。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實際建築的設計。","textEn":"Design exercise: a historic building weighing W = 216,000 kN is isolated on 54 lead-rubber bearings. For one bearing, a 150 mm lead core with 10 MPa yield stress gives Q_d ≈ 177 kN, and a 900 mm diameter with 200 mm total rubber and G = 0.4 MPa gives K_d ≈ 1,237 kN/m. At the design displacement D = 0.40 m, F ≈ 672 kN, K_eff ≈ 1,679 kN/m and β_eff ≈ 16%. The system K ≈ 90,650 kN/m gives T = 2π√(W/(g·K)) ≈ 3.1 s; with S_D1 = 0.7 and B = 1.35, D = g·S_D1·T/(4π²·B) ≈ 9.81×0.7×3.1/(39.48×1.35) ≈ 0.40 m, consistent with the assumption, and the base-shear coefficient is about 0.17, roughly one sixth of the fixed-base value. For a 60 m × 30 m plan with 3 m eccentricity the corner displacement is about 0.50 m, so the moat should be at least 0.55 m. Upper-bound properties (Q_d×1.3, K_d×1.1) raise the bearing force to about 774 kN, about 15% more superstructure force; a moat reduced to 0.30 m means an impact energy of about 3.2 MJ. Values are teaching assumptions, not the design of any real building.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b077-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「週期延長與隔震改造的動機」與「隔震面位置、扭轉放大與隔震縫」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Period lengthening and why to isolate an existing building\" and \"Isolation-plane location, torsional amplification and the moat\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b077-v13-01","title":"週期延長與隔震改造的動機：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Period lengthening and why to isolate an existing building: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「隔震層週期」如何影響既有建築基礎隔震改造的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Isolated period” governs force, deformation or durability in “Base-isolation retrofit of existing buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"許多既有建築，尤其是無筋磚造或石造的歷史建築，強度與韌性都不足，以傳統方式加剪力牆或斜撐，會大量破壞內部裝飾與空間。基礎隔震改從需求端下手：在建築下方插入水平柔軟的隔震層，把系統週期由約 0.5 s 延長到 2 至 3 s 以上，地震加速度大幅降低，上部結構幾乎以剛體平移，變形集中在隔震層。代價是隔震層要容納數十公分的位移，並需處理建築周邊的隔震縫與穿越管線。Forell/Elsesser 指出，鹽湖城市郡大樓是全球第一個以基礎隔震改造的既有建築。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「隔震層週期」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Many existing buildings, especially unreinforced masonry or stone landmarks, lack strength and ductility, and conventional strengthening with shear walls or braces would destroy much of their interior fabric. Base isolation attacks demand instead: a laterally flexible isolation layer inserted beneath the building lengthens the period from about 0.5 s to 2 to 3 s or more, sharply reducing earthquake acceleration so that the superstructure moves almost as a rigid body while deformation concentrates in the isolation layer. The price is that the layer must accommodate tens of centimetres of displacement, with a moat around the building and flexible utility crossings. Forell/Elsesser describes the Salt Lake City and County Building as the world's first base-isolation retrofit of an existing building. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Isolated period” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：T = 2π√(W/(g·K_eff))。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: T = 2π√(W/(g·K_eff)).","failure":"常見誤解：「隔震改造會讓建築在地震中完全不動。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Base isolation makes a building stay completely still in an earthquake.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「隔震層週期」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Isolated period”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-01-k1","title":"週期延長與隔震改造的動機","titleEn":"Period lengthening and why to isolate an existing building","text":"許多既有建築，尤其是無筋磚造或石造的歷史建築，強度與韌性都不足，以傳統方式加剪力牆或斜撐，會大量破壞內部裝飾與空間。基礎隔震改從需求端下手：在建築下方插入水平柔軟的隔震層，把系統週期由約 0.5 s 延長到 2 至 3 s 以上，地震加速度大幅降低，上部結構幾乎以剛體平移，變形集中在隔震層。","textEn":"Many existing buildings, especially unreinforced masonry or stone landmarks, lack strength and ductility, and conventional strengthening with shear walls or braces would destroy much of their interior fabric. Base isolation attacks demand instead: a laterally flexible isolation layer inserted beneath the building lengthens the period from about 0.5 s to 2 to 3 s or more, sharply reducing earthquake acceleration so that the superstructure moves almost as a rigid body while deformation concentrates in the isolation layer.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：隔震改造會讓建築在地震中完全不動。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Base isolation makes a building stay completely still in an earthquake. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「週期延長與隔震改造的動機」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Period lengthening and why to isolate an existing building\" is correct?","options":["隔震改造會讓建築在地震中完全不動。","許多既有建築，尤其是無筋磚造或石造的歷史建築，強度與韌性都不足，以傳統方式加剪力牆或斜撐，會大量破壞內部裝飾與空間。","隔震縫寬度只要等於設計位移即可，不必考慮扭轉。"],"optionsEn":["Base isolation makes a building stay completely still in an earthquake.","Many existing buildings, especially unreinforced masonry or stone landmarks, lack strength and ductility, and conventional strengthening with shear walls or braces would destroy much of their interior fabric.","The moat width only needs to equal the design displacement, without considering torsion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"許多既有建築，尤其是無筋磚造或石造的歷史建築，強度與韌性都不足，以傳統方式加剪力牆或斜撐，會大量破壞內部裝飾與空間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Many existing buildings, especially unreinforced masonry or stone landmarks, lack strength and ductility, and conventional strengthening with shear walls or braces would destroy much of their interior fabric. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b077-v13-02","title":"週期延長與隔震改造的動機：定量估算","titleEn":"Period lengthening and why to isolate an existing building: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「隔震層週期」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Isolated period” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：T = 2π√(W/(g·K_eff))。W = 216,000 kN、54 個隔震器各 K_eff ≈ 1,679 kN/m（K ≈ 90,650 kN/m），T = 2π√(216,000/(9.81×90,650)) ≈ 3.1 s。以 S_D1 = 0.7、阻尼修正 B = 1.35，基底剪力係數 S_D1/(T·B) = 0.7/(3.1×1.35) ≈ 0.17，而固定基底 0.5 s 時約為 1.0，約降為六分之一。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: T = 2π√(W/(g·K_eff)). With W = 216,000 kN and 54 isolators of K_eff ≈ 1,679 kN/m each (K ≈ 90,650 kN/m), T = 2π√(216,000/(9.81×90,650)) ≈ 3.1 s. With S_D1 = 0.7 and damping coefficient B = 1.35, the base-shear coefficient is S_D1/(T·B) = 0.7/(3.1×1.35) ≈ 0.17, against about 1.0 for the fixed base at 0.5 s, roughly one sixth. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以既有建築調查得到的材料強度與重量建立模型，比較固定基底與隔震兩種方案的樓層加速度、層間變位與上部結構需求強度比；同時評估場址是否為軟弱土層或近斷層，因為長週期地動會削弱隔震效益，必要時做場址反應分析。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build a model from surveyed material strengths and weights, compare floor accelerations, drifts and superstructure demand-to-capacity ratios for fixed-base and isolated schemes, and check whether the site is soft soil or near-fault, since long-period ground motion erodes the benefit, performing site-response analysis where needed.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"T = 2π√(W/(g·K_eff))。W = 216,000 kN、54 個隔震器各 K_eff ≈ 1,679 kN/m（K ≈ 90,650 kN/m），T = 2π√(216,000/(9.81×90,650)) ≈ 3.1 s。以 S_D1 = 0.7、阻尼修正 B = 1.35，基底剪力係數 S_D1/(T·B) = 0.7/(3.1×1.35) ≈ 0.17，而固定基底 0.5 s 時約為 1.0，約降為六分之一。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"T = 2π√(W/(g·K_eff)). With W = 216,000 kN and 54 isolators of K_eff ≈ 1,679 kN/m each (K ≈ 90,650 kN/m), T = 2π√(216,000/(9.81×90,650)) ≈ 3.1 s. With S_D1 = 0.7 and damping coefficient B = 1.35, the base-shear coefficient is S_D1/(T·B) = 0.7/(3.1×1.35) ≈ 0.17, against about 1.0 for the fixed base at 0.5 s, roughly one sixth. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「週期延長與隔震改造的動機」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Period lengthening and why to isolate an existing building\", which statement holds?","options":["新澆托換梁只要與舊柱接觸，就能自動把柱荷載傳過去。","施工期間只有幾年，不需要考慮地震。","T = 2π√(W/(g·K_eff))。"],"optionsEn":["A newly cast transfer beam that touches the old column will automatically pick up its load.","Construction lasts only a few years, so earthquakes need not be considered.","T = 2π√(W/(g·K_eff))."],"answer":2,"explanation":"T = 2π√(W/(g·K_eff))。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"T = 2π√(W/(g·K_eff)). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b077-v13-03","title":"週期延長與隔震改造的動機：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Period lengthening and why to isolate an existing building: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「隔震層週期」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Isolated period” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以既有建築調查得到的材料強度與重量建立模型，比較固定基底與隔震兩種方案的樓層加速度、層間變位與上部結構需求強度比；同時評估場址是否為軟弱土層或近斷層，因為長週期地動會削弱隔震效益，必要時做場址反應分析。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build a model from surveyed material strengths and weights, compare floor accelerations, drifts and superstructure demand-to-capacity ratios for fixed-base and isolated schemes, and check whether the site is soft soil or near-fault, since long-period ground motion erodes the benefit, performing site-response analysis where needed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：可行性研究階段就要比較隔震與傳統補強在文化資產衝擊、停用期間、造價與性能目標上的差異，並把性能目標（例如震後立即使用）寫進設計基準由業主確認。","observationEn":"Site practice: At feasibility stage compare isolation with conventional strengthening for heritage impact, closure time, cost and performance, and write the performance objective, for example immediate occupancy after the earthquake, into the design basis for the owner to confirm.","failure":"注意干擾：若在軟弱土層上隔震而未做場址分析，地動的長週期能量正好落在隔震週期附近，位移遠超過預期，撞擊隔震縫邊牆；若上部結構過於柔軟或有軟弱層，變形不會只集中在隔震層，仍可能損傷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Isolating on soft soil without site analysis can put long-period ground-motion energy right at the isolated period, so displacement far exceeds expectations and the building strikes the moat wall; a flexible superstructure or soft storey keeps deformation from concentrating in the isolation layer and still allows damage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以既有建築調查得到的材料強度與重量建立模型，比較固定基底與隔震兩種方案的樓層加速度、層間變位與上部結構需求強度比；同時評估場址是否為軟弱土層或近斷層，因為長週期地動會削弱隔震效益，必要時做場址反應分析。","textEn":"Build a model from surveyed material strengths and weights, compare floor accelerations, drifts and superstructure demand-to-capacity ratios for fixed-base and isolated schemes, and check whether the site is soft soil or near-fault, since long-period ground motion erodes the benefit, performing site-response analysis where needed.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"可行性研究階段就要比較隔震與傳統補強在文化資產衝擊、停用期間、造價與性能目標上的差異，並把性能目標（例如震後立即使用）寫進設計基準由業主確認。","textEn":"At feasibility stage compare isolation with conventional strengthening for heritage impact, closure time, cost and performance, and write the performance objective, for example immediate occupancy after the earthquake, into the design basis for the owner to confirm.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「週期延長與隔震改造的動機」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Period lengthening and why to isolate an existing building\"?","options":["以既有建築調查得到的材料強度與重量建立模型，比較固定基底與隔震兩種方案的樓層加速度、層間變位與上部結構需求強度比。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","小地震時隔震建築的加速度折減應該和設計地震一樣大。"],"optionsEn":["Build a model from surveyed material strengths and weights, compare floor accelerations, drifts and superstructure demand-to-capacity ratios for fixed-base and isolated schemes, and check whether the site is soft soil or near-fault, since long-period ground motion erodes the benefit, performing site-response analysis where needed.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","In a small earthquake an isolated building should show the same acceleration reduction as in the design earthquake."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以既有建築調查得到的材料強度與重量建立模型，比較固定基底與隔震兩種方案的樓層加速度、層間變位與上部結構需求強度比；同時評估場址是否為軟弱土層或近斷層，因為長週期地動會削弱隔震效益，必要時做場址反應分析。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build a model from surveyed material strengths and weights, compare floor accelerations, drifts and superstructure demand-to-capacity ratios for fixed-base and isolated schemes, and check whether the site is soft soil or near-fault, since long-period ground motion erodes the benefit, performing site-response analysis where needed. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b077-v13-04","title":"週期延長與隔震改造的動機：失效診斷","titleEn":"Period lengthening and why to isolate an existing building: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「隔震層週期」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Isolated period” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若在軟弱土層上隔震而未做場址分析，地動的長週期能量正好落在隔震週期附近，位移遠超過預期，撞擊隔震縫邊牆；若上部結構過於柔軟或有軟弱層，變形不會只集中在隔震層，仍可能損傷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Isolating on soft soil without site analysis can put long-period ground-motion energy right at the isolated period, so displacement far exceeds expectations and the building strikes the moat wall; a flexible superstructure or soft storey keeps deformation from concentrating in the isolation layer and still allows damage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：Forell/Elsesser 指出，鹽湖城市郡大樓是全球第一個以基礎隔震改造的既有建築。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Forell/Elsesser describes the Salt Lake City and County Building as the world's first base-isolation retrofit of an existing building.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「隔震改造會讓建築在地震中完全不動。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Base isolation makes a building stay completely still in an earthquake.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若在軟弱土層上隔震而未做場址分析，地動的長週期能量正好落在隔震週期附近，位移遠超過預期，撞擊隔震縫邊牆；若上部結構過於柔軟或有軟弱層，變形不會只集中在隔震層，仍可能損傷。","textEn":"Isolating on soft soil without site analysis can put long-period ground-motion energy right at the isolated period, so displacement far exceeds expectations and the building strikes the moat wall; a flexible superstructure or soft storey keeps deformation from concentrating in the isolation layer and still allows damage.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「週期延長與隔震改造的動機」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Period lengthening and why to isolate an existing building\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若在軟弱土層上隔震而未做場址分析，地動的長週期能量正好落在隔震週期附近，位移遠超過預期，撞擊隔震縫邊牆。","隔震縫寬度只要等於設計位移即可，不必考慮扭轉。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Isolating on soft soil without site analysis can put long-period ground-motion energy right at the isolated period, so displacement far exceeds expectations and the building strikes the moat wall.","The moat width only needs to equal the design displacement, without considering torsion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若在軟弱土層上隔震而未做場址分析，地動的長週期能量正好落在隔震週期附近，位移遠超過預期，撞擊隔震縫邊牆；若上部結構過於柔軟或有軟弱層，變形不會只集中在隔震層，仍可能損傷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Isolating on soft soil without site analysis can put long-period ground-motion energy right at the isolated period, so displacement far exceeds expectations and the building strikes the moat wall; a flexible superstructure or soft storey keeps deformation from concentrating in the isolation layer and still allows damage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b077-v13-05","title":"隔震面位置、扭轉放大與隔震縫：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Isolation-plane location, torsional amplification and the moat: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「隔震縫與隔震面」如何影響既有建築基礎隔震改造的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Moat and isolation plane” governs force, deformation or durability in “Base-isolation retrofit of existing buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"改造時隔震面的位置決定了工程難度：放在地下室底部要開挖並托換基礎，放在地下室柱頂則地下室仍隨地盤運動。隔震面正上方必須有一層剛性樓板或格梁，把各柱連成整體，讓所有隔震器同步變形。建築的質心與隔震層勁度中心若不重合，扭轉會使角落隔震器的位移大於中心，所以隔震縫寬度要按最大總位移而非平均位移設計，並保留所有穿越管線與通道的可動接頭。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「隔震縫與隔震面」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The location of the isolation plane governs the difficulty of a retrofit: at the base of the basement it requires excavation and underpinning, while at basement column tops the basement still moves with the ground. A stiff diaphragm or grid of beams is needed directly above the isolators to tie the columns together so that all isolators deform together. If the centre of mass does not coincide with the centre of isolator stiffness, torsion makes corner isolators move more than central ones, so the moat must be sized for the total maximum displacement rather than the average, with movable joints for every utility and access crossing. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Moat and isolation plane” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以 ASCE 7-10 型式的扭轉放大 D_TM = D_M·[1 + y·12e/(b² + d²)]。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Using the ASCE 7-10 form of torsional amplification, D_TM = D_M·[1 + y·12e/(b² + d²)].","failure":"常見誤解：「隔震縫寬度只要等於設計位移即可，不必考慮扭轉。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The moat width only needs to equal the design displacement, without considering torsion.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「隔震縫與隔震面」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Moat and isolation plane”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-05-k1","title":"隔震面位置、扭轉放大與隔震縫","titleEn":"Isolation-plane location, torsional amplification and the moat","text":"改造時隔震面的位置決定了工程難度：放在地下室底部要開挖並托換基礎，放在地下室柱頂則地下室仍隨地盤運動。隔震面正上方必須有一層剛性樓板或格梁，把各柱連成整體，讓所有隔震器同步變形。","textEn":"The location of the isolation plane governs the difficulty of a retrofit: at the base of the basement it requires excavation and underpinning, while at basement column tops the basement still moves with the ground. A stiff diaphragm or grid of beams is needed directly above the isolators to tie the columns together so that all isolators deform together.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：隔震縫寬度只要等於設計位移即可，不必考慮扭轉。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The moat width only needs to equal the design displacement, without considering torsion. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「隔震面位置、扭轉放大與隔震縫」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Isolation-plane location, torsional amplification and the moat\" is correct?","options":["隔震縫寬度只要等於設計位移即可，不必考慮扭轉。","隔震支承的勁度與阻尼是固定值，不隨位移改變。","改造時隔震面的位置決定了工程難度：放在地下室底部要開挖並托換基礎，放在地下室柱頂則地下室仍隨地盤運動。"],"optionsEn":["The moat width only needs to equal the design displacement, without considering torsion.","An isolator's stiffness and damping are fixed values that do not change with displacement.","The location of the isolation plane governs the difficulty of a retrofit: at the base of the basement it requires excavation and underpinning, while at basement column tops the basement still moves with the ground."],"answer":2,"explanation":"改造時隔震面的位置決定了工程難度：放在地下室底部要開挖並托換基礎，放在地下室柱頂則地下室仍隨地盤運動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The location of the isolation plane governs the difficulty of a retrofit: at the base of the basement it requires excavation and underpinning, while at basement column tops the basement still moves with the ground. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b077-v13-06","title":"隔震面位置、扭轉放大與隔震縫：定量估算","titleEn":"Isolation-plane location, torsional amplification and the moat: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「隔震縫與隔震面」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Moat and isolation plane” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以 ASCE 7-10 型式的扭轉放大 D_TM = D_M·[1 + y·12e/(b² + d²)]。平面 60 m × 30 m、偶然偏心 e = 5%×60 = 3 m、角落距離 y = 30 m：12×3×30/(3,600+900) = 0.24，D_M = 0.40 m 時 D_TM ≈ 0.40×1.24 ≈ 0.50 m，隔震縫淨寬取 0.55 m 以上。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Using the ASCE 7-10 form of torsional amplification, D_TM = D_M·[1 + y·12e/(b² + d²)]. For a 60 m × 30 m plan, accidental eccentricity e = 5%×60 = 3 m and corner distance y = 30 m: 12×3×30/(3,600+900) = 0.24, so D_M = 0.40 m gives D_TM ≈ 0.40×1.24 ≈ 0.50 m and the moat clear width should be at least 0.55 m. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以三維模型做雙向地震的非線性時間歷程分析，檢查每個隔震器的最大位移、最大與最小軸力（含上浮），並確認隔震縫、樓梯、電梯坑與管線在最大總位移下不碰撞；設計圖上逐一標示各穿越點的允許位移量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Run three-dimensional nonlinear time-history analysis with bidirectional records to check each isolator's maximum displacement and maximum and minimum axial force, including uplift, and confirm that the moat, stairs, lift pits and utilities do not collide at the total maximum displacement; mark the allowable movement at every crossing on the drawings.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以 ASCE 7-10 型式的扭轉放大 D_TM = D_M·[1 + y·12e/(b² + d²)]。平面 60 m × 30 m、偶然偏心 e = 5%×60 = 3 m、角落距離 y = 30 m：12×3×30/(3,600+900) = 0.24，D_M = 0.40 m 時 D_TM ≈ 0.40×1.24 ≈ 0.50 m，隔震縫淨寬取 0.55 m 以上。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Using the ASCE 7-10 form of torsional amplification, D_TM = D_M·[1 + y·12e/(b² + d²)]. For a 60 m × 30 m plan, accidental eccentricity e = 5%×60 = 3 m and corner distance y = 30 m: 12×3×30/(3,600+900) = 0.24, so D_M = 0.40 m gives D_TM ≈ 0.40×1.24 ≈ 0.50 m and the moat clear width should be at least 0.55 m. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「隔震面位置、扭轉放大與隔震縫」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Isolation-plane location, torsional amplification and the moat\", which statement holds?","options":["以 ASCE 7-10 型式的扭轉放大 D_TM = D_M·[1 + y·12e/(b² + d²)]。","切柱只是施工手續，只要千斤頂撐住就不會影響上部結構。","隔震器只要在慢速試驗中合格，地震時的性質就一定相同。"],"optionsEn":["Using the ASCE 7-10 form of torsional amplification, D_TM = D_M·[1 + y·12e/(b² + d²)].","Cutting columns is a routine step; as long as jacks hold them, the superstructure is unaffected.","If an isolator passes slow-speed tests, its properties in an earthquake will be the same."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以 ASCE 7-10 型式的扭轉放大 D_TM = D_M·[1 + y·12e/(b² + d²)]。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Using the ASCE 7-10 form of torsional amplification, D_TM = D_M·[1 + y·12e/(b² + d²)]. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b077-v13-07","title":"隔震面位置、扭轉放大與隔震縫：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Isolation-plane location, torsional amplification and the moat: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「隔震縫與隔震面」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Moat and isolation plane” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以三維模型做雙向地震的非線性時間歷程分析，檢查每個隔震器的最大位移、最大與最小軸力（含上浮），並確認隔震縫、樓梯、電梯坑與管線在最大總位移下不碰撞；設計圖上逐一標示各穿越點的允許位移量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Run three-dimensional nonlinear time-history analysis with bidirectional records to check each isolator's maximum displacement and maximum and minimum axial force, including uplift, and confirm that the moat, stairs, lift pits and utilities do not collide at the total maximum displacement; mark the allowable movement at every crossing on the drawings. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：隔震縫的蓋板、伸縮踏板與管線可動接頭應列入圖說與驗收項目，並在現場以油漆或標牌標示「隔震縫內不得堆放或施作」；任何穿越隔震面的新設施都須經結構技師核可。","observationEn":"Site practice: Moat covers, sliding treads and flexible utility joints should be shown on drawings and included in acceptance, and the moat should be marked on site as a no-storage, no-construction zone; any new item crossing the isolation plane needs the structural engineer's approval.","failure":"注意干擾：隔震縫寬度只按中心位移設計時，角落在強震中撞擊擋土牆，撞擊產生的高頻加速度與剪力傳回上部結構，抵銷隔震效益；隔震面上方缺乏剛性樓板，各隔震器不同步變形，部分柱承受額外彎矩。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A moat sized for the central displacement lets corners strike the retaining wall in a strong earthquake, sending high-frequency acceleration and shear back into the superstructure and cancelling the isolation benefit; without a stiff diaphragm above, isolators deform unevenly and some columns pick up extra moment. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以三維模型做雙向地震的非線性時間歷程分析，檢查每個隔震器的最大位移、最大與最小軸力（含上浮），並確認隔震縫、樓梯、電梯坑與管線在最大總位移下不碰撞；設計圖上逐一標示各穿越點的允許位移量。","textEn":"Run three-dimensional nonlinear time-history analysis with bidirectional records to check each isolator's maximum displacement and maximum and minimum axial force, including uplift, and confirm that the moat, stairs, lift pits and utilities do not collide at the total maximum displacement; mark the allowable movement at every crossing on the drawings.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"隔震縫的蓋板、伸縮踏板與管線可動接頭應列入圖說與驗收項目，並在現場以油漆或標牌標示「隔震縫內不得堆放或施作」；任何穿越隔震面的新設施都須經結構技師核可。","textEn":"Moat covers, sliding treads and flexible utility joints should be shown on drawings and included in acceptance, and the moat should be marked on site as a no-storage, no-construction zone; any new item crossing the isolation plane needs the structural engineer's approval.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「隔震面位置、扭轉放大與隔震縫」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Isolation-plane location, torsional amplification and the moat\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以三維模型做雙向地震的非線性時間歷程分析，檢查每個隔震器的最大位移、最大與最小軸力（含上浮），並確認隔震縫、樓梯、電梯坑與管線在最大總位移下不碰撞。","只要用試驗量到的名目性質分析，隔震設計就涵蓋了全部情況。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Run three-dimensional nonlinear time-history analysis with bidirectional records to check each isolator's maximum displacement and maximum and minimum axial force, including uplift, and confirm that the moat, stairs, lift pits and utilities do not collide at the total maximum displacement.","Analysing with the nominal tested properties covers every case in isolation design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以三維模型做雙向地震的非線性時間歷程分析，檢查每個隔震器的最大位移、最大與最小軸力（含上浮），並確認隔震縫、樓梯、電梯坑與管線在最大總位移下不碰撞；設計圖上逐一標示各穿越點的允許位移量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Run three-dimensional nonlinear time-history analysis with bidirectional records to check each isolator's maximum displacement and maximum and minimum axial force, including uplift, and confirm that the moat, stairs, lift pits and utilities do not collide at the total maximum displacement; mark the allowable movement at every crossing on the drawings. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b077-v13-08","title":"隔震面位置、扭轉放大與隔震縫：失效診斷","titleEn":"Isolation-plane location, torsional amplification and the moat: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「隔震縫與隔震面」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Moat and isolation plane” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"隔震縫寬度只按中心位移設計時，角落在強震中撞擊擋土牆，撞擊產生的高頻加速度與剪力傳回上部結構，抵銷隔震效益；隔震面上方缺乏剛性樓板，各隔震器不同步變形，部分柱承受額外彎矩。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A moat sized for the central displacement lets corners strike the retaining wall in a strong earthquake, sending high-frequency acceleration and shear back into the superstructure and cancelling the isolation benefit; without a stiff diaphragm above, isolators deform unevenly and some columns pick up extra moment. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：建築的質心與隔震層勁度中心若不重合，扭轉會使角落隔震器的位移大於中心，所以隔震縫寬度要按最大總位移而非平均位移設計，並保留所有穿越管線與通道的可動接頭。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If the centre of mass does not coincide with the centre of isolator stiffness, torsion makes corner isolators move more than central ones, so the moat must be sized for the total maximum displacement rather than the average, with movable joints for every utility and access crossing.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「隔震縫寬度只要等於設計位移即可，不必考慮扭轉。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The moat width only needs to equal the design displacement, without considering torsion.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"隔震縫寬度只按中心位移設計時，角落在強震中撞擊擋土牆，撞擊產生的高頻加速度與剪力傳回上部結構，抵銷隔震效益；隔震面上方缺乏剛性樓板，各隔震器不同步變形，部分柱承受額外彎矩。","textEn":"A moat sized for the central displacement lets corners strike the retaining wall in a strong earthquake, sending high-frequency acceleration and shear back into the superstructure and cancelling the isolation benefit; without a stiff diaphragm above, isolators deform unevenly and some columns pick up extra moment.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「隔震面位置、扭轉放大與隔震縫」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Isolation-plane location, torsional amplification and the moat\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","隔震支承的勁度與阻尼是固定值，不隨位移改變。","隔震縫寬度只按中心位移設計時，角落在強震中撞擊擋土牆，撞擊產生的高頻加速度與剪力傳回上部結構，抵銷隔震效益。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","An isolator's stiffness and damping are fixed values that do not change with displacement.","A moat sized for the central displacement lets corners strike the retaining wall in a strong earthquake, sending high-frequency acceleration and shear back into the superstructure and cancelling the isolation benefit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"隔震縫寬度只按中心位移設計時，角落在強震中撞擊擋土牆，撞擊產生的高頻加速度與剪力傳回上部結構，抵銷隔震效益；隔震面上方缺乏剛性樓板，各隔震器不同步變形，部分柱承受額外彎矩。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A moat sized for the central displacement lets corners strike the retaining wall in a strong earthquake, sending high-frequency acceleration and shear back into the superstructure and cancelling the isolation benefit; without a stiff diaphragm above, isolators deform unevenly and some columns pick up extra moment. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b077-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「鉛心橡膠支承的雙線性性質」與「托換梁與既有基礎的荷載轉移」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Bilinear properties of lead-rubber bearings\" and \"Transfer girders and load transfer from existing foundations\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b077-v13-09","title":"鉛心橡膠支承的雙線性性質：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Bilinear properties of lead-rubber bearings: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「鉛心橡膠支承」如何影響既有建築基礎隔震改造的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lead-rubber bearing” governs force, deformation or durability in “Base-isolation retrofit of existing buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"鉛心橡膠支承由多層薄橡膠與鋼板交錯硫化而成，中心插入鉛棒：鋼板限制橡膠的側向膨脹，使支承在垂直方向很硬、水平方向很軟；鉛心在小位移時提供初始勁度與抗風強度，降伏後以塑性變形耗能，力—位移關係近似雙線性。設計參數包括鉛心特性強度 Q_d、降伏後勁度 K_d（由橡膠剪力模數、面積與總厚度決定）、有效勁度與等效阻尼比，這些值都隨位移改變。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「鉛心橡膠支承」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A lead-rubber bearing is built from thin rubber layers vulcanised between steel shims with a lead plug at its centre: the shims restrain lateral bulging so the bearing is very stiff vertically and soft horizontally, while the lead core provides initial stiffness and wind resistance at small displacement and, after yielding, dissipates energy by plastic deformation, giving a roughly bilinear force–displacement curve. Design parameters are the characteristic strength Q_d of the lead, the post-yield stiffness K_d set by rubber shear modulus, area and total thickness, the effective stiffness and the equivalent damping ratio, all of which vary with displacement. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Lead-rubber bearing” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：鉛心直徑 150 mm、鉛降伏應力 10 MPa：Q_d = 10×π/4×150² ≈ 177 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A 150 mm lead core with 10 MPa yield stress gives Q_d = 10×π/4×150² ≈ 177 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「隔震支承的勁度與阻尼是固定值，不隨位移改變。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An isolator's stiffness and damping are fixed values that do not change with displacement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「鉛心橡膠支承」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Lead-rubber bearing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-09-k1","title":"鉛心橡膠支承的雙線性性質","titleEn":"Bilinear properties of lead-rubber bearings","text":"鉛心橡膠支承由多層薄橡膠與鋼板交錯硫化而成，中心插入鉛棒：鋼板限制橡膠的側向膨脹，使支承在垂直方向很硬、水平方向很軟；鉛心在小位移時提供初始勁度與抗風強度，降伏後以塑性變形耗能，力—位移關係近似雙線性。設計參數包括鉛心特性強度 Q_d、降伏後勁度 K_d（由橡膠剪力模數、面積與總厚度決定）、有效勁度與等效阻尼比，這些值都隨位移改變。","textEn":"A lead-rubber bearing is built from thin rubber layers vulcanised between steel shims with a lead plug at its centre: the shims restrain lateral bulging so the bearing is very stiff vertically and soft horizontally, while the lead core provides initial stiffness and wind resistance at small displacement and, after yielding, dissipates energy by plastic deformation, giving a roughly bilinear force–displacement curve. Design parameters are the characteristic strength Q_d of the lead, the post-yield stiffness K_d set by rubber shear modulus, area and total thickness, the effective stiffness and the equivalent damping ratio, all of which vary with displacement.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：隔震支承的勁度與阻尼是固定值，不隨位移改變。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An isolator's stiffness and damping are fixed values that do not change with displacement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鉛心橡膠支承的雙線性性質」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bilinear properties of lead-rubber bearings\" is correct?","options":["鉛心橡膠支承由多層薄橡膠與鋼板交錯硫化而成，中心插入鉛棒：鋼板限制橡膠的側向膨脹，使支承在垂直方向很硬、水平方向很軟。","隔震支承的勁度與阻尼是固定值，不隨位移改變。","新澆托換梁只要與舊柱接觸，就能自動把柱荷載傳過去。"],"optionsEn":["A lead-rubber bearing is built from thin rubber layers vulcanised between steel shims with a lead plug at its centre: the shims restrain lateral bulging so the bearing is very stiff vertically and soft horizontally, while the lead core provides initial stiffness and wind resistance at small displacement and, after yielding, dissipates energy by plastic deformation, giving a roughly bilinear force–displacement curve.","An isolator's stiffness and damping are fixed values that do not change with displacement.","A newly cast transfer beam that touches the old column will automatically pick up its load."],"answer":0,"explanation":"鉛心橡膠支承由多層薄橡膠與鋼板交錯硫化而成，中心插入鉛棒：鋼板限制橡膠的側向膨脹，使支承在垂直方向很硬、水平方向很軟；鉛心在小位移時提供初始勁度與抗風強度，降伏後以塑性變形耗能，力—位移關係近似雙線性。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A lead-rubber bearing is built from thin rubber layers vulcanised between steel shims with a lead plug at its centre: the shims restrain lateral bulging so the bearing is very stiff vertically and soft horizontally, while the lead core provides initial stiffness and wind resistance at small displacement and, after yielding, dissipates energy by plastic deformation, giving a roughly bilinear force–displacement curve. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b077-v13-10","title":"鉛心橡膠支承的雙線性性質：定量估算","titleEn":"Bilinear properties of lead-rubber bearings: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鉛心橡膠支承」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lead-rubber bearing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：鉛心直徑 150 mm、鉛降伏應力 10 MPa：Q_d = 10×π/4×150² ≈ 177 kN。支承直徑 900 mm、橡膠總厚 200 mm、G = 0.4 MPa：A_r ≈ 0.619 m²，K_d = G·A_r/t_r ≈ 1,237 kN/m。D = 0.40 m 時 F = 177 + 1,237×0.40 ≈ 672 kN，K_eff ≈ 1,679 kN/m；EDC ≈ 4×177×(0.40−0.02) ≈ 269 kJ，β_eff = EDC/(2π·K_eff·D²) ≈ 16%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A 150 mm lead core with 10 MPa yield stress gives Q_d = 10×π/4×150² ≈ 177 kN. A 900 mm bearing with 200 mm total rubber and G = 0.4 MPa has A_r ≈ 0.619 m² and K_d = G·A_r/t_r ≈ 1,237 kN/m. At D = 0.40 m, F = 177 + 1,237×0.40 ≈ 672 kN and K_eff ≈ 1,679 kN/m; EDC ≈ 4×177×(0.40−0.02) ≈ 269 kJ and β_eff = EDC/(2π·K_eff·D²) ≈ 16%. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：依 ISO 22762 或 ASCE 7 隔震章節的精神，以原型試驗量測不同位移下的 Q_d、K_d、K_eff 與 EDC，並檢查垂直勁度、在最大位移下的穩定性與上浮行為；橡膠材料另做剪力模數、硬度與老化試驗。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: In the spirit of ISO 22762 and the isolation chapter of ASCE 7, prototype tests measure Q_d, K_d, K_eff and EDC at several displacements and check vertical stiffness, stability at maximum displacement and uplift behaviour; rubber compounds are also tested for shear modulus, hardness and ageing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"鉛心直徑 150 mm、鉛降伏應力 10 MPa：Q_d = 10×π/4×150² ≈ 177 kN。支承直徑 900 mm、橡膠總厚 200 mm、G = 0.4 MPa：A_r ≈ 0.619 m²，K_d = G·A_r/t_r ≈ 1,237 kN/m。D = 0.40 m 時 F = 177 + 1,237×0.40 ≈ 672 kN，K_eff ≈ 1,679 kN/m；EDC ≈ 4×177×(0.40−0.02) ≈ 269 kJ，β_eff = EDC/(2π·K_eff·D²) ≈ 16%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A 150 mm lead core with 10 MPa yield stress gives Q_d = 10×π/4×150² ≈ 177 kN. A 900 mm bearing with 200 mm total rubber and G = 0.4 MPa has A_r ≈ 0.619 m² and K_d = G·A_r/t_r ≈ 1,237 kN/m. At D = 0.40 m, F = 177 + 1,237×0.40 ≈ 672 kN and K_eff ≈ 1,679 kN/m; EDC ≈ 4×177×(0.40−0.02) ≈ 269 kJ and β_eff = EDC/(2π·K_eff·D²) ≈ 16%. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鉛心橡膠支承的雙線性性質」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bilinear properties of lead-rubber bearings\", which statement holds?","options":["施工期間只有幾年，不需要考慮地震。","鉛心直徑 150 mm、鉛降伏應力 10 MPa：Q_d = 10×π/4×150² ≈ 177 kN。","小地震時隔震建築的加速度折減應該和設計地震一樣大。"],"optionsEn":["Construction lasts only a few years, so earthquakes need not be considered.","A 150 mm lead core with 10 MPa yield stress gives Q_d = 10×π/4×150² ≈ 177 kN.","In a small earthquake an isolated building should show the same acceleration reduction as in the design earthquake."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鉛心直徑 150 mm、鉛降伏應力 10 MPa：Q_d = 10×π/4×150² ≈ 177 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A 150 mm lead core with 10 MPa yield stress gives Q_d = 10×π/4×150² ≈ 177 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b077-v13-11","title":"鉛心橡膠支承的雙線性性質：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bilinear properties of lead-rubber bearings: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鉛心橡膠支承」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lead-rubber bearing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"依 ISO 22762 或 ASCE 7 隔震章節的精神，以原型試驗量測不同位移下的 Q_d、K_d、K_eff 與 EDC，並檢查垂直勁度、在最大位移下的穩定性與上浮行為；橡膠材料另做剪力模數、硬度與老化試驗。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"In the spirit of ISO 22762 and the isolation chapter of ASCE 7, prototype tests measure Q_d, K_d, K_eff and EDC at several displacements and check vertical stiffness, stability at maximum displacement and uplift behaviour; rubber compounds are also tested for shear modulus, hardness and ageing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：規格書要列出每種支承在設計與最大位移下的 K_eff、EDC 與允收偏差，並要求每個支承有序號與試驗紀錄；同一隔震層盡量減少支承種類，避免安裝時錯置。","observationEn":"Site practice: The specification should list K_eff, EDC and tolerances at design and maximum displacement for each bearing type, with a serial number and test record for every bearing; keep the number of bearing types in one isolation layer small to avoid mix-ups during installation.","failure":"注意干擾：若支承在最大位移下的重疊面積太小，加上大軸力，橡膠層會失穩或撕裂；鋼板與橡膠的黏結不良，則在反覆剪力下逐層剝離，支承勁度與承載力下降。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If the overlap area at maximum displacement is too small under high axial load, the rubber layers can become unstable or tear; poor bonding between shims and rubber leads to layer-by-layer delamination under cyclic shear, reducing stiffness and capacity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"依 ISO 22762 或 ASCE 7 隔震章節的精神，以原型試驗量測不同位移下的 Q_d、K_d、K_eff 與 EDC，並檢查垂直勁度、在最大位移下的穩定性與上浮行為；橡膠材料另做剪力模數、硬度與老化試驗。","textEn":"In the spirit of ISO 22762 and the isolation chapter of ASCE 7, prototype tests measure Q_d, K_d, K_eff and EDC at several displacements and check vertical stiffness, stability at maximum displacement and uplift behaviour; rubber compounds are also tested for shear modulus, hardness and ageing.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"規格書要列出每種支承在設計與最大位移下的 K_eff、EDC 與允收偏差，並要求每個支承有序號與試驗紀錄；同一隔震層盡量減少支承種類，避免安裝時錯置。","textEn":"The specification should list K_eff, EDC and tolerances at design and maximum displacement for each bearing type, with a serial number and test record for every bearing; keep the number of bearing types in one isolation layer small to avoid mix-ups during installation.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鉛心橡膠支承的雙線性性質」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bilinear properties of lead-rubber bearings\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","隔震改造完成後，隔震縫只是一條空隙，不需要維護。","依 ISO 22762 或 ASCE 7 隔震章節的精神，以原型試驗量測不同位移下的 Q_d、K_d、K_eff 與 EDC，並檢查垂直勁度、在最大位移下的穩定性與上浮行為。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Once the retrofit is complete, the moat is just a gap that needs no maintenance.","In the spirit of ISO 22762 and the isolation chapter of ASCE 7, prototype tests measure Q_d, K_d, K_eff and EDC at several displacements and check vertical stiffness, stability at maximum displacement and uplift behaviour."],"answer":2,"explanation":"依 ISO 22762 或 ASCE 7 隔震章節的精神，以原型試驗量測不同位移下的 Q_d、K_d、K_eff 與 EDC，並檢查垂直勁度、在最大位移下的穩定性與上浮行為；橡膠材料另做剪力模數、硬度與老化試驗。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"In the spirit of ISO 22762 and the isolation chapter of ASCE 7, prototype tests measure Q_d, K_d, K_eff and EDC at several displacements and check vertical stiffness, stability at maximum displacement and uplift behaviour; rubber compounds are also tested for shear modulus, hardness and ageing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b077-v13-12","title":"鉛心橡膠支承的雙線性性質：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bilinear properties of lead-rubber bearings: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鉛心橡膠支承」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lead-rubber bearing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若支承在最大位移下的重疊面積太小，加上大軸力，橡膠層會失穩或撕裂；鋼板與橡膠的黏結不良，則在反覆剪力下逐層剝離，支承勁度與承載力下降。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If the overlap area at maximum displacement is too small under high axial load, the rubber layers can become unstable or tear; poor bonding between shims and rubber leads to layer-by-layer delamination under cyclic shear, reducing stiffness and capacity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：設計參數包括鉛心特性強度 Q_d、降伏後勁度 K_d（由橡膠剪力模數、面積與總厚度決定）、有效勁度與等效阻尼比，這些值都隨位移改變。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Design parameters are the characteristic strength Q_d of the lead, the post-yield stiffness K_d set by rubber shear modulus, area and total thickness, the effective stiffness and the equivalent damping ratio, all of which vary with displacement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「隔震支承的勁度與阻尼是固定值，不隨位移改變。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An isolator's stiffness and damping are fixed values that do not change with displacement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若支承在最大位移下的重疊面積太小，加上大軸力，橡膠層會失穩或撕裂；鋼板與橡膠的黏結不良，則在反覆剪力下逐層剝離，支承勁度與承載力下降。","textEn":"If the overlap area at maximum displacement is too small under high axial load, the rubber layers can become unstable or tear; poor bonding between shims and rubber leads to layer-by-layer delamination under cyclic shear, reducing stiffness and capacity.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鉛心橡膠支承的雙線性性質」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bilinear properties of lead-rubber bearings\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若支承在最大位移下的重疊面積太小，加上大軸力，橡膠層會失穩或撕裂；鋼板與橡膠的黏結不良，則在反覆剪力下逐層剝離，支承勁度與承載力下降。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","新澆托換梁只要與舊柱接觸，就能自動把柱荷載傳過去。"],"optionsEn":["If the overlap area at maximum displacement is too small under high axial load, the rubber layers can become unstable or tear.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A newly cast transfer beam that touches the old column will automatically pick up its load."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若支承在最大位移下的重疊面積太小，加上大軸力，橡膠層會失穩或撕裂；鋼板與橡膠的黏結不良，則在反覆剪力下逐層剝離，支承勁度與承載力下降。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If the overlap area at maximum displacement is too small under high axial load, the rubber layers can become unstable or tear; poor bonding between shims and rubber leads to layer-by-layer delamination under cyclic shear, reducing stiffness and capacity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b077-v13-13","title":"托換梁與既有基礎的荷載轉移：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Transfer girders and load transfer from existing foundations: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「後拉預力托換梁」如何影響既有建築基礎隔震改造的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Post-tensioned transfer girder” governs force, deformation or durability in “Base-isolation retrofit of existing buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"改造的關鍵是如何在不移除建築的前提下，把每根柱或每道牆的重量從原基礎轉到新隔震器上。常見做法是在柱或牆兩側澆置新的混凝土托換梁或夾套，以後拉預力把新舊混凝土夾緊，靠摩擦與剪力榫把荷載傳入新構件，再由新構件坐在隔震器上。Forell/Elsesser 的猶他州議會大廈改造即以環繞既有墩基礎的後拉預力混凝土大梁形成複合斷面，跨距約 51 ft，把約 28,000,000 lb 的荷載轉到新隔震器，避免在既有基礎下方開挖。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「後拉預力托換梁」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The key to a retrofit is moving the weight of every column or wall from the old foundation onto new isolators without removing the building. A common method casts new concrete transfer beams or jackets on both sides of a column or wall and clamps new to old concrete with post-tensioning, so that friction and shear keys carry the load into the new members, which then sit on the isolators. In the Utah State Capitol retrofit, Forell/Elsesser wrapped the existing pier footings with post-tensioned concrete girders forming composite sections, spanning about 51 ft, to transfer about 28,000,000 lb onto new isolators without excavating beneath the old footings. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Post-tensioned transfer girder” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以摩擦轉移柱荷載 P = 2·μ·N（兩側夾板）。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Transferring a column load by friction, P = 2·μ·N for two clamping faces.","failure":"常見誤解：「新澆托換梁只要與舊柱接觸，就能自動把柱荷載傳過去。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A newly cast transfer beam that touches the old column will automatically pick up its load.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「後拉預力托換梁」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Post-tensioned transfer girder”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-13-k1","title":"托換梁與既有基礎的荷載轉移","titleEn":"Transfer girders and load transfer from existing foundations","text":"改造的關鍵是如何在不移除建築的前提下，把每根柱或每道牆的重量從原基礎轉到新隔震器上。常見做法是在柱或牆兩側澆置新的混凝土托換梁或夾套，以後拉預力把新舊混凝土夾緊，靠摩擦與剪力榫把荷載傳入新構件，再由新構件坐在隔震器上。","textEn":"The key to a retrofit is moving the weight of every column or wall from the old foundation onto new isolators without removing the building. A common method casts new concrete transfer beams or jackets on both sides of a column or wall and clamps new to old concrete with post-tensioning, so that friction and shear keys carry the load into the new members, which then sit on the isolators.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：新澆托換梁只要與舊柱接觸，就能自動把柱荷載傳過去。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A newly cast transfer beam that touches the old column will automatically pick up its load. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「托換梁與既有基礎的荷載轉移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Transfer girders and load transfer from existing foundations\" is correct?","options":["新澆托換梁只要與舊柱接觸，就能自動把柱荷載傳過去。","改造的關鍵是如何在不移除建築的前提下，把每根柱或每道牆的重量從原基礎轉到新隔震器上。","切柱只是施工手續，只要千斤頂撐住就不會影響上部結構。"],"optionsEn":["A newly cast transfer beam that touches the old column will automatically pick up its load.","The key to a retrofit is moving the weight of every column or wall from the old foundation onto new isolators without removing the building.","Cutting columns is a routine step; as long as jacks hold them, the superstructure is unaffected."],"answer":1,"explanation":"改造的關鍵是如何在不移除建築的前提下，把每根柱或每道牆的重量從原基礎轉到新隔震器上。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The key to a retrofit is moving the weight of every column or wall from the old foundation onto new isolators without removing the building. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b077-v13-14","title":"托換梁與既有基礎的荷載轉移：定量估算","titleEn":"Transfer girders and load transfer from existing foundations: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「後拉預力托換梁」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Post-tensioned transfer girder” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以摩擦轉移柱荷載 P = 2·μ·N（兩側夾板）。P = 4,000 kN、粗糙面摩擦係數 μ = 0.7 時，所需夾緊力 N = 4,000/(2×0.7) ≈ 2,857 kN；15.2 mm 鋼絞線（140 mm²、f_pu = 1,860 MPa）以 0.6 f_pu 計每股約 156 kN，需 2,857/156 ≈ 18.3，取 19 股。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Transferring a column load by friction, P = 2·μ·N for two clamping faces. With P = 4,000 kN and a roughened-surface friction coefficient μ = 0.7, the clamping force is N = 4,000/(2×0.7) ≈ 2,857 kN; a 15.2 mm strand (140 mm², f_pu = 1,860 MPa) at 0.6 f_pu gives about 156 kN, so 2,857/156 ≈ 18.3, rounded up to 19 strands. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：施工前鑽心確認既有混凝土強度與粗糙化處理後的介面，必要時做介面剪力試驗；預力施加時記錄每束伸長量與千斤頂壓力並比對計算值，偏差超過允許值（例如 ±7%）須停工檢討。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before construction, core the existing concrete to confirm strength and the roughened interface, with interface shear tests where needed; during stressing, record elongation and jack pressure for every tendon against calculated values and stop to investigate if deviations exceed tolerance, for example ±7%.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以摩擦轉移柱荷載 P = 2·μ·N（兩側夾板）。P = 4,000 kN、粗糙面摩擦係數 μ = 0.7 時，所需夾緊力 N = 4,000/(2×0.7) ≈ 2,857 kN；15.2 mm 鋼絞線（140 mm²、f_pu = 1,860 MPa）以 0.6 f_pu 計每股約 156 kN，需 2,857/156 ≈ 18.3，取 19 股。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Transferring a column load by friction, P = 2·μ·N for two clamping faces. With P = 4,000 kN and a roughened-surface friction coefficient μ = 0.7, the clamping force is N = 4,000/(2×0.7) ≈ 2,857 kN; a 15.2 mm strand (140 mm², f_pu = 1,860 MPa) at 0.6 f_pu gives about 156 kN, so 2,857/156 ≈ 18.3, rounded up to 19 strands. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「托換梁與既有基礎的荷載轉移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Transfer girders and load transfer from existing foundations\", which statement holds?","options":["隔震器只要在慢速試驗中合格，地震時的性質就一定相同。","只要用試驗量到的名目性質分析，隔震設計就涵蓋了全部情況。","以摩擦轉移柱荷載 P = 2·μ·N（兩側夾板）。"],"optionsEn":["If an isolator passes slow-speed tests, its properties in an earthquake will be the same.","Analysing with the nominal tested properties covers every case in isolation design.","Transferring a column load by friction, P = 2·μ·N for two clamping faces."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以摩擦轉移柱荷載 P = 2·μ·N（兩側夾板）。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Transferring a column load by friction, P = 2·μ·N for two clamping faces. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b077-v13-15","title":"托換梁與既有基礎的荷載轉移：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Transfer girders and load transfer from existing foundations: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「後拉預力托換梁」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Post-tensioned transfer girder” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"施工前鑽心確認既有混凝土強度與粗糙化處理後的介面，必要時做介面剪力試驗；預力施加時記錄每束伸長量與千斤頂壓力並比對計算值，偏差超過允許值（例如 ±7%）須停工檢討。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before construction, core the existing concrete to confirm strength and the roughened interface, with interface shear tests where needed; during stressing, record elongation and jack pressure for every tendon against calculated values and stop to investigate if deviations exceed tolerance, for example ±7%. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：荷載轉移構件的界面處理、剪力榫、預力束配置與量測紀錄表都應列為停止點，並由結構技師現場確認後才可進行下一步切柱或頂升。","observationEn":"Site practice: Interface preparation, shear keys, tendon layout and measurement sheets for transfer members should be hold points, confirmed on site by the structural engineer before any column cutting or jacking proceeds.","failure":"注意干擾：若既有混凝土強度低於假設或介面清理不足，摩擦轉移不足，荷載轉移時新舊混凝土間發生滑動，柱突然下沉並拉裂上部磚牆；預力損失估計過低，則長期夾緊力下降，轉移構件逐漸滑移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If the existing concrete is weaker than assumed or the interface poorly prepared, friction is insufficient and new and old concrete slip during transfer, dropping the column suddenly and cracking masonry above; underestimated prestress losses let clamping fall over time so that the transfer member gradually slips. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"施工前鑽心確認既有混凝土強度與粗糙化處理後的介面，必要時做介面剪力試驗；預力施加時記錄每束伸長量與千斤頂壓力並比對計算值，偏差超過允許值（例如 ±7%）須停工檢討。","textEn":"Before construction, core the existing concrete to confirm strength and the roughened interface, with interface shear tests where needed; during stressing, record elongation and jack pressure for every tendon against calculated values and stop to investigate if deviations exceed tolerance, for example ±7%.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"荷載轉移構件的界面處理、剪力榫、預力束配置與量測紀錄表都應列為停止點，並由結構技師現場確認後才可進行下一步切柱或頂升。","textEn":"Interface preparation, shear keys, tendon layout and measurement sheets for transfer members should be hold points, confirmed on site by the structural engineer before any column cutting or jacking proceeds.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「托換梁與既有基礎的荷載轉移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Transfer girders and load transfer from existing foundations\"?","options":["施工前鑽心確認既有混凝土強度與粗糙化處理後的介面，必要時做介面剪力試驗。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","隔震改造會讓建築在地震中完全不動。"],"optionsEn":["Before construction, core the existing concrete to confirm strength and the roughened interface, with interface shear tests where needed.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Base isolation makes a building stay completely still in an earthquake."],"answer":0,"explanation":"施工前鑽心確認既有混凝土強度與粗糙化處理後的介面，必要時做介面剪力試驗；預力施加時記錄每束伸長量與千斤頂壓力並比對計算值，偏差超過允許值（例如 ±7%）須停工檢討。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before construction, core the existing concrete to confirm strength and the roughened interface, with interface shear tests where needed; during stressing, record elongation and jack pressure for every tendon against calculated values and stop to investigate if deviations exceed tolerance, for example ±7%. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b077-v13-16","title":"托換梁與既有基礎的荷載轉移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Transfer girders and load transfer from existing foundations: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「後拉預力托換梁」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Post-tensioned transfer girder” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若既有混凝土強度低於假設或介面清理不足，摩擦轉移不足，荷載轉移時新舊混凝土間發生滑動，柱突然下沉並拉裂上部磚牆；預力損失估計過低，則長期夾緊力下降，轉移構件逐漸滑移。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If the existing concrete is weaker than assumed or the interface poorly prepared, friction is insufficient and new and old concrete slip during transfer, dropping the column suddenly and cracking masonry above; underestimated prestress losses let clamping fall over time so that the transfer member gradually slips. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：Forell/Elsesser 的猶他州議會大廈改造即以環繞既有墩基礎的後拉預力混凝土大梁形成複合斷面，跨距約 51 ft，把約 28,000,000 lb 的荷載轉到新隔震器，避免在既有基礎下方開挖。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: In the Utah State Capitol retrofit, Forell/Elsesser wrapped the existing pier footings with post-tensioned concrete girders forming composite sections, spanning about 51 ft, to transfer about 28,000,000 lb onto new isolators without excavating beneath the old footings.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「新澆托換梁只要與舊柱接觸，就能自動把柱荷載傳過去。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A newly cast transfer beam that touches the old column will automatically pick up its load.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若既有混凝土強度低於假設或介面清理不足，摩擦轉移不足，荷載轉移時新舊混凝土間發生滑動，柱突然下沉並拉裂上部磚牆；預力損失估計過低，則長期夾緊力下降，轉移構件逐漸滑移。","textEn":"If the existing concrete is weaker than assumed or the interface poorly prepared, friction is insufficient and new and old concrete slip during transfer, dropping the column suddenly and cracking masonry above; underestimated prestress losses let clamping fall over time so that the transfer member gradually slips.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「托換梁與既有基礎的荷載轉移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Transfer girders and load transfer from existing foundations\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若既有混凝土強度低於假設或介面清理不足，摩擦轉移不足，荷載轉移時新舊混凝土間發生滑動，柱突然下沉並拉裂上部磚牆。","切柱只是施工手續，只要千斤頂撐住就不會影響上部結構。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","If the existing concrete is weaker than assumed or the interface poorly prepared, friction is insufficient and new and old concrete slip during transfer, dropping the column suddenly and cracking masonry above.","Cutting columns is a routine step; as long as jacks hold them, the superstructure is unaffected."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若既有混凝土強度低於假設或介面清理不足，摩擦轉移不足，荷載轉移時新舊混凝土間發生滑動，柱突然下沉並拉裂上部磚牆；預力損失估計過低，則長期夾緊力下降，轉移構件逐漸滑移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If the existing concrete is weaker than assumed or the interface poorly prepared, friction is insufficient and new and old concrete slip during transfer, dropping the column suddenly and cracking masonry above; underestimated prestress losses let clamping fall over time so that the transfer member gradually slips. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b077-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「切柱、頂升與沉陷控制」與「施工期間的暫態結構與地震風險」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cutting, jacking and settlement control\" and \"Temporary structural states and earthquake risk during construction\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b077-v13-17","title":"切柱、頂升與沉陷控制：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Cutting, jacking and settlement control: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「切柱頂升與臨時支撐」如何影響既有建築基礎隔震改造的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Column cutting, jacking and shoring” governs force, deformation or durability in “Base-isolation retrofit of existing buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"隔震器就位前，柱或牆必須被切斷，荷載暫時由千斤頂與臨時支撐承擔，再把千斤頂壓力轉到隔震器上。舊金山市政府的改造中，約 530 根柱與約 1,500 ft 的厚重磚牆被切斷並暫時頂撐，才能安裝隔震器。歷史建築對差異沉陷極為敏感，數毫米的差異就可能使灰泥裝飾開裂，因此要以千斤頂預壓抵銷隔震器受壓後的垂直變形，並按事先排定的順序逐柱施作。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「切柱頂升與臨時支撐」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Before an isolator goes in, a column or wall must be cut, its load carried temporarily by jacks and shoring, and the jack pressure then transferred onto the isolator. In the San Francisco City Hall retrofit about 530 columns and about 1,500 ft of massive brick walls were cut and temporarily jacked so that isolators could be installed. Historic buildings are very sensitive to differential settlement, where a few millimetres can crack plaster ornament, so jacks preload to offset the isolator's vertical compression, and columns are done one by one in a planned sequence. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Column cutting, jacking and shoring” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：單層橡膠厚 10 mm 時形狀係數 S = 900/(4×10) = 22.5，壓縮模數近似 E_c ≈ 6·G·S² = 6×0.4×22.5² ≈ 1,215 MPa，垂直勁度 K_v = E_c·A_r/t_r ≈ 1,215,000×0.619/0.2 ≈ 3.76×10⁶ kN/m；柱荷載 4,000 kN 時壓縮約 1.1 mm，須以千斤頂預壓抵銷。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With 10 mm rubber layers the shape factor is S = 900/(4×10) = 22.5, the compression modulus is roughly E_c ≈ 6·G·S² = 6×0.4×22.5² ≈ 1,215 MPa and the vertical stiffness K_v = E_c·A_r/t_r ≈ 1,215,000×0.619/0.2 ≈ 3.76×10⁶ kN/m; a 4,000 kN column load compresses the bearing about 1.1 mm, which jack preload must offset.","failure":"常見誤解：「切柱只是施工手續，只要千斤頂撐住就不會影響上部結構。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Cutting columns is a routine step; as long as jacks hold them, the superstructure is unaffected.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「切柱頂升與臨時支撐」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Column cutting, jacking and shoring”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-17-k1","title":"切柱、頂升與沉陷控制","titleEn":"Cutting, jacking and settlement control","text":"隔震器就位前，柱或牆必須被切斷，荷載暫時由千斤頂與臨時支撐承擔，再把千斤頂壓力轉到隔震器上。舊金山市政府的改造中，約 530 根柱與約 1,500 ft 的厚重磚牆被切斷並暫時頂撐，才能安裝隔震器。","textEn":"Before an isolator goes in, a column or wall must be cut, its load carried temporarily by jacks and shoring, and the jack pressure then transferred onto the isolator. In the San Francisco City Hall retrofit about 530 columns and about 1,500 ft of massive brick walls were cut and temporarily jacked so that isolators could be installed.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：切柱只是施工手續，只要千斤頂撐住就不會影響上部結構。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Cutting columns is a routine step; as long as jacks hold them, the superstructure is unaffected. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「切柱、頂升與沉陷控制」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cutting, jacking and settlement control\" is correct?","options":["切柱只是施工手續，只要千斤頂撐住就不會影響上部結構。","施工期間只有幾年，不需要考慮地震。","隔震器就位前，柱或牆必須被切斷，荷載暫時由千斤頂與臨時支撐承擔，再把千斤頂壓力轉到隔震器上。"],"optionsEn":["Cutting columns is a routine step; as long as jacks hold them, the superstructure is unaffected.","Construction lasts only a few years, so earthquakes need not be considered.","Before an isolator goes in, a column or wall must be cut, its load carried temporarily by jacks and shoring, and the jack pressure then transferred onto the isolator."],"answer":2,"explanation":"隔震器就位前，柱或牆必須被切斷，荷載暫時由千斤頂與臨時支撐承擔，再把千斤頂壓力轉到隔震器上。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Before an isolator goes in, a column or wall must be cut, its load carried temporarily by jacks and shoring, and the jack pressure then transferred onto the isolator. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b077-v13-18","title":"切柱、頂升與沉陷控制：定量估算","titleEn":"Cutting, jacking and settlement control: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「切柱頂升與臨時支撐」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Column cutting, jacking and shoring” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：單層橡膠厚 10 mm 時形狀係數 S = 900/(4×10) = 22.5，壓縮模數近似 E_c ≈ 6·G·S² = 6×0.4×22.5² ≈ 1,215 MPa，垂直勁度 K_v = E_c·A_r/t_r ≈ 1,215,000×0.619/0.2 ≈ 3.76×10⁶ kN/m；柱荷載 4,000 kN 時壓縮約 1.1 mm，須以千斤頂預壓抵銷。數值為教學假設，未計體積壓縮修正。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With 10 mm rubber layers the shape factor is S = 900/(4×10) = 22.5, the compression modulus is roughly E_c ≈ 6·G·S² = 6×0.4×22.5² ≈ 1,215 MPa and the vertical stiffness K_v = E_c·A_r/t_r ≈ 1,215,000×0.619/0.2 ≈ 3.76×10⁶ kN/m; a 4,000 kN column load compresses the bearing about 1.1 mm, which jack preload must offset. Values are teaching assumptions without bulk-compressibility correction. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每根柱在切斷前、頂升中與轉移後以精密水準儀量測高程，並在千斤頂上記錄壓力；相鄰柱的差異沉陷超過允許值（例如 3 mm）即停止並調整，裂縫監測計與傾斜計同步記錄磚牆反應。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Level every column with a precise level before cutting, during jacking and after transfer, recording jack pressures; stop and adjust if differential settlement between neighbouring columns exceeds the limit, for example 3 mm, while crack gauges and tiltmeters record the masonry's response.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"單層橡膠厚 10 mm 時形狀係數 S = 900/(4×10) = 22.5，壓縮模數近似 E_c ≈ 6·G·S² = 6×0.4×22.5² ≈ 1,215 MPa，垂直勁度 K_v = E_c·A_r/t_r ≈ 1,215,000×0.619/0.2 ≈ 3.76×10⁶ kN/m；柱荷載 4,000 kN 時壓縮約 1.1 mm，須以千斤頂預壓抵銷。數值為教學假設，未計體積壓縮修正。","textEn":"With 10 mm rubber layers the shape factor is S = 900/(4×10) = 22.5, the compression modulus is roughly E_c ≈ 6·G·S² = 6×0.4×22.5² ≈ 1,215 MPa and the vertical stiffness K_v = E_c·A_r/t_r ≈ 1,215,000×0.619/0.2 ≈ 3.76×10⁶ kN/m; a 4,000 kN column load compresses the bearing about 1.1 mm, which jack preload must offset. Values are teaching assumptions without bulk-compressibility correction.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「切柱、頂升與沉陷控制」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cutting, jacking and settlement control\", which statement holds?","options":["單層橡膠厚 10 mm 時形狀係數 S = 900/(4×10) = 22.5，壓縮模數近似 E_c ≈ 6·G·S² = 6×0.4×22.5² ≈ 1,215 MPa，垂直勁度 K_v = E_c·A_r/t_r ≈ 1,215,000×0.619/0.2 ≈ 3.76×10⁶ kN/m。","小地震時隔震建築的加速度折減應該和設計地震一樣大。","隔震改造完成後，隔震縫只是一條空隙，不需要維護。"],"optionsEn":["With 10 mm rubber layers the shape factor is S = 900/(4×10) = 22.5, the compression modulus is roughly E_c ≈ 6·G·S² = 6×0.4×22.5² ≈ 1,215 MPa and the vertical stiffness K_v = E_c·A_r/t_r ≈ 1,215,000×0.619/0.2 ≈ 3.76×10⁶ kN/m.","In a small earthquake an isolated building should show the same acceleration reduction as in the design earthquake.","Once the retrofit is complete, the moat is just a gap that needs no maintenance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"單層橡膠厚 10 mm 時形狀係數 S = 900/(4×10) = 22.5，壓縮模數近似 E_c ≈ 6·G·S² = 6×0.4×22.5² ≈ 1,215 MPa，垂直勁度 K_v = E_c·A_r/t_r ≈ 1,215,000×0.619/0.2 ≈ 3.76×10⁶ kN/m；柱荷載 4,000 kN 時壓縮約 1.1 mm，須以千斤頂預壓抵銷。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With 10 mm rubber layers the shape factor is S = 900/(4×10) = 22.5, the compression modulus is roughly E_c ≈ 6·G·S² = 6×0.4×22.5² ≈ 1,215 MPa and the vertical stiffness K_v = E_c·A_r/t_r ≈ 1,215,000×0.619/0.2 ≈ 3.76×10⁶ kN/m; a 4,000 kN column load compresses the bearing about 1.1 mm, which jack preload must offset. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b077-v13-19","title":"切柱、頂升與沉陷控制：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cutting, jacking and settlement control: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「切柱頂升與臨時支撐」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Column cutting, jacking and shoring” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每根柱在切斷前、頂升中與轉移後以精密水準儀量測高程，並在千斤頂上記錄壓力；相鄰柱的差異沉陷超過允許值（例如 3 mm）即停止並調整，裂縫監測計與傾斜計同步記錄磚牆反應。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Level every column with a precise level before cutting, during jacking and after transfer, recording jack pressures; stop and adjust if differential settlement between neighbouring columns exceeds the limit, for example 3 mm, while crack gauges and tiltmeters record the masonry's response. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：施工計畫要列出切柱順序、同時切斷柱數上限、千斤頂預壓值、沉陷與裂縫的停止條件，以及臨時支撐的側向設計，由結構技師簽認並設為每一柱的停止點；這些步驟是工程推理與檢核，不是現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: The construction plan should list the cutting sequence, the maximum number of columns cut at once, jack preloads, stop criteria for settlement and cracking, and the lateral design of shoring, signed by the structural engineer as a hold point for every column; these steps are engineering reasoning and checks, not a field operating permit.","failure":"注意干擾：若一次切斷太多相鄰柱或千斤頂壓力不一致，荷載在臨時系統中重分配，部分柱瞬間下沉，造成磚牆與拱頂開裂；臨時支撐若只承受垂直力，施工中的地震或施工機具撞擊可能使其側向失穩。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Cutting too many adjacent columns at once or uneven jack pressures redistribute load within the temporary system, so some columns drop suddenly and crack masonry walls and vaults; shoring designed only for vertical load can become laterally unstable under a construction-period earthquake or equipment impact. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每根柱在切斷前、頂升中與轉移後以精密水準儀量測高程，並在千斤頂上記錄壓力；相鄰柱的差異沉陷超過允許值（例如 3 mm）即停止並調整，裂縫監測計與傾斜計同步記錄磚牆反應。","textEn":"Level every column with a precise level before cutting, during jacking and after transfer, recording jack pressures; stop and adjust if differential settlement between neighbouring columns exceeds the limit, for example 3 mm, while crack gauges and tiltmeters record the masonry's response.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"施工計畫要列出切柱順序、同時切斷柱數上限、千斤頂預壓值、沉陷與裂縫的停止條件，以及臨時支撐的側向設計，由結構技師簽認並設為每一柱的停止點；這些步驟是工程推理與檢核，不是現場操作許可。","textEn":"The construction plan should list the cutting sequence, the maximum number of columns cut at once, jack preloads, stop criteria for settlement and cracking, and the lateral design of shoring, signed by the structural engineer as a hold point for every column; these steps are engineering reasoning and checks, not a field operating permit.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「切柱、頂升與沉陷控制」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cutting, jacking and settlement control\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","每根柱在切斷前、頂升中與轉移後以精密水準儀量測高程，並在千斤頂上記錄壓力。","隔震縫寬度只要等於設計位移即可，不必考慮扭轉。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Level every column with a precise level before cutting, during jacking and after transfer, recording jack pressures.","The moat width only needs to equal the design displacement, without considering torsion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每根柱在切斷前、頂升中與轉移後以精密水準儀量測高程，並在千斤頂上記錄壓力；相鄰柱的差異沉陷超過允許值（例如 3 mm）即停止並調整，裂縫監測計與傾斜計同步記錄磚牆反應。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Level every column with a precise level before cutting, during jacking and after transfer, recording jack pressures; stop and adjust if differential settlement between neighbouring columns exceeds the limit, for example 3 mm, while crack gauges and tiltmeters record the masonry's response. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b077-v13-20","title":"切柱、頂升與沉陷控制：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cutting, jacking and settlement control: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「切柱頂升與臨時支撐」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Column cutting, jacking and shoring” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若一次切斷太多相鄰柱或千斤頂壓力不一致，荷載在臨時系統中重分配，部分柱瞬間下沉，造成磚牆與拱頂開裂；臨時支撐若只承受垂直力，施工中的地震或施工機具撞擊可能使其側向失穩。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Cutting too many adjacent columns at once or uneven jack pressures redistribute load within the temporary system, so some columns drop suddenly and crack masonry walls and vaults; shoring designed only for vertical load can become laterally unstable under a construction-period earthquake or equipment impact. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：歷史建築對差異沉陷極為敏感，數毫米的差異就可能使灰泥裝飾開裂，因此要以千斤頂預壓抵銷隔震器受壓後的垂直變形，並按事先排定的順序逐柱施作。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Historic buildings are very sensitive to differential settlement, where a few millimetres can crack plaster ornament, so jacks preload to offset the isolator's vertical compression, and columns are done one by one in a planned sequence.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「切柱只是施工手續，只要千斤頂撐住就不會影響上部結構。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Cutting columns is a routine step; as long as jacks hold them, the superstructure is unaffected.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若一次切斷太多相鄰柱或千斤頂壓力不一致，荷載在臨時系統中重分配，部分柱瞬間下沉，造成磚牆與拱頂開裂；臨時支撐若只承受垂直力，施工中的地震或施工機具撞擊可能使其側向失穩。","textEn":"Cutting too many adjacent columns at once or uneven jack pressures redistribute load within the temporary system, so some columns drop suddenly and crack masonry walls and vaults; shoring designed only for vertical load can become laterally unstable under a construction-period earthquake or equipment impact.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「切柱、頂升與沉陷控制」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cutting, jacking and settlement control\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","施工期間只有幾年，不需要考慮地震。","若一次切斷太多相鄰柱或千斤頂壓力不一致，荷載在臨時系統中重分配，部分柱瞬間下沉，造成磚牆與拱頂開裂。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Construction lasts only a few years, so earthquakes need not be considered.","Cutting too many adjacent columns at once or uneven jack pressures redistribute load within the temporary system, so some columns drop suddenly and crack masonry walls and vaults."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若一次切斷太多相鄰柱或千斤頂壓力不一致，荷載在臨時系統中重分配，部分柱瞬間下沉，造成磚牆與拱頂開裂；臨時支撐若只承受垂直力，施工中的地震或施工機具撞擊可能使其側向失穩。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Cutting too many adjacent columns at once or uneven jack pressures redistribute load within the temporary system, so some columns drop suddenly and crack masonry walls and vaults; shoring designed only for vertical load can become laterally unstable under a construction-period earthquake or equipment impact. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b077-v13-21","title":"施工期間的暫態結構與地震風險：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Temporary structural states and earthquake risk during construction: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「施工期間地震風險」如何影響既有建築基礎隔震改造的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Construction-period earthquake risk” governs force, deformation or durability in “Base-isolation retrofit of existing buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"改造期間建築處在最脆弱的狀態：部分柱已切斷、隔震器尚未全部就位、隔震縫還沒完成，原本的基礎與新系統都只是半套。Forell/Elsesser 說明舊金山市政府的施工排序，目的之一就是在施工期間萬一發生地震時仍維持結構穩定。設計者必須把每個施工階段當成一個暫態結構，決定其要承受的地震水準，並以臨時側向束制、限制同時施工範圍或分區施作來控制風險。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「施工期間地震風險」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"During a retrofit the building is at its most vulnerable: some columns are cut, not all isolators are in place and the moat is unfinished, so neither the old foundation nor the new system is complete. Forell/Elsesser explains that construction sequencing at San Francisco City Hall aimed, among other things, to keep the structure stable should an earthquake strike during the work. Designers must treat each construction stage as a temporary structure, choose the earthquake level it must resist, and control risk with temporary lateral restraints, limits on simultaneous work areas or zoned construction. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Construction-period earthquake risk” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：施工期間發生某回歸期地震的機率 P = 1 − exp(−t/T_R)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The probability of an earthquake of a given return period during construction is P = 1 − exp(−t/T_R).","failure":"常見誤解：「施工期間只有幾年，不需要考慮地震。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Construction lasts only a few years, so earthquakes need not be considered.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「施工期間地震風險」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Construction-period earthquake risk”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-21-k1","title":"施工期間的暫態結構與地震風險","titleEn":"Temporary structural states and earthquake risk during construction","text":"改造期間建築處在最脆弱的狀態：部分柱已切斷、隔震器尚未全部就位、隔震縫還沒完成，原本的基礎與新系統都只是半套。Forell/Elsesser 說明舊金山市政府的施工排序，目的之一就是在施工期間萬一發生地震時仍維持結構穩定。","textEn":"During a retrofit the building is at its most vulnerable: some columns are cut, not all isolators are in place and the moat is unfinished, so neither the old foundation nor the new system is complete. Forell/Elsesser explains that construction sequencing at San Francisco City Hall aimed, among other things, to keep the structure stable should an earthquake strike during the work.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：施工期間只有幾年，不需要考慮地震。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Construction lasts only a few years, so earthquakes need not be considered. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「施工期間的暫態結構與地震風險」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Temporary structural states and earthquake risk during construction\" is correct?","options":["改造期間建築處在最脆弱的狀態：部分柱已切斷、隔震器尚未全部就位、隔震縫還沒完成，原本的基礎與新系統都只是半套。","施工期間只有幾年，不需要考慮地震。","隔震器只要在慢速試驗中合格，地震時的性質就一定相同。"],"optionsEn":["During a retrofit the building is at its most vulnerable: some columns are cut, not all isolators are in place and the moat is unfinished, so neither the old foundation nor the new system is complete.","Construction lasts only a few years, so earthquakes need not be considered.","If an isolator passes slow-speed tests, its properties in an earthquake will be the same."],"answer":0,"explanation":"改造期間建築處在最脆弱的狀態：部分柱已切斷、隔震器尚未全部就位、隔震縫還沒完成，原本的基礎與新系統都只是半套。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"During a retrofit the building is at its most vulnerable: some columns are cut, not all isolators are in place and the moat is unfinished, so neither the old foundation nor the new system is complete. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b077-v13-22","title":"施工期間的暫態結構與地震風險：定量估算","titleEn":"Temporary structural states and earthquake risk during construction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「施工期間地震風險」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Construction-period earthquake risk” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：施工期間發生某回歸期地震的機率 P = 1 − exp(−t/T_R)。工期 t = 3 年：對 475 年回歸期 P = 1 − exp(−3/475) ≈ 0.63%；對 72 年回歸期 P ≈ 1 − exp(−3/72) ≈ 4.1%，所以暫態結構至少要能安全承受較常發生的中小地震。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The probability of an earthquake of a given return period during construction is P = 1 − exp(−t/T_R). For t = 3 years: a 475-year event gives P = 1 − exp(−3/475) ≈ 0.63%, and a 72-year event P ≈ 1 − exp(−3/72) ≈ 4.1%, so temporary states must at least safely resist the more frequent moderate earthquakes. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：為每個施工階段建立模型，檢查在選定的施工期地震下，臨時支撐、已切柱位與未完成區的側向強度與變形；施工中每週更新已完成與未完成的柱位圖，確認實際進度沒有超出分析過的暫態組合。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Model each construction stage and check the lateral strength and deformation of shoring, cut-column locations and unfinished zones under the selected construction-period earthquake; update a weekly plan of completed and pending column positions to confirm that actual progress stays within the analysed temporary states.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"施工期間發生某回歸期地震的機率 P = 1 − exp(−t/T_R)。工期 t = 3 年：對 475 年回歸期 P = 1 − exp(−3/475) ≈ 0.63%；對 72 年回歸期 P ≈ 1 − exp(−3/72) ≈ 4.1%，所以暫態結構至少要能安全承受較常發生的中小地震。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"The probability of an earthquake of a given return period during construction is P = 1 − exp(−t/T_R). For t = 3 years: a 475-year event gives P = 1 − exp(−3/475) ≈ 0.63%, and a 72-year event P ≈ 1 − exp(−3/72) ≈ 4.1%, so temporary states must at least safely resist the more frequent moderate earthquakes. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「施工期間的暫態結構與地震風險」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Temporary structural states and earthquake risk during construction\", which statement holds?","options":["只要用試驗量到的名目性質分析，隔震設計就涵蓋了全部情況。","施工期間發生某回歸期地震的機率 P = 1 − exp(−t/T_R)。","隔震改造會讓建築在地震中完全不動。"],"optionsEn":["Analysing with the nominal tested properties covers every case in isolation design.","The probability of an earthquake of a given return period during construction is P = 1 − exp(−t/T_R).","Base isolation makes a building stay completely still in an earthquake."],"answer":1,"explanation":"施工期間發生某回歸期地震的機率 P = 1 − exp(−t/T_R)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The probability of an earthquake of a given return period during construction is P = 1 − exp(−t/T_R). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b077-v13-23","title":"施工期間的暫態結構與地震風險：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Temporary structural states and earthquake risk during construction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「施工期間地震風險」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Construction-period earthquake risk” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"為每個施工階段建立模型，檢查在選定的施工期地震下，臨時支撐、已切柱位與未完成區的側向強度與變形；施工中每週更新已完成與未完成的柱位圖，確認實際進度沒有超出分析過的暫態組合。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Model each construction stage and check the lateral strength and deformation of shoring, cut-column locations and unfinished zones under the selected construction-period earthquake; update a weekly plan of completed and pending column positions to confirm that actual progress stays within the analysed temporary states. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：合約應規定施工期地震的設計水準、同時施作範圍上限與緊急應變程序，地震後先由結構技師檢查臨時系統才可復工；進度變更須先送設計者評估暫態安全。","observationEn":"Site practice: The contract should set the construction-period design earthquake, the maximum simultaneous work area and an emergency procedure, with work resuming after an earthquake only once the structural engineer has inspected the temporary system; any change in sequence must first go to the designer for temporary-state assessment.","failure":"注意干擾：若施工單位為趕工而同時切斷超出計畫的柱數，結構進入沒有分析過的暫態，中度地震就可能使臨時支撐傾倒；隔震器已安裝但尚未完成隔震縫時，建築撞上開挖面的臨時擋土，也可能造成損傷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If the contractor cuts more columns than planned to save time, the structure enters an unanalysed temporary state in which a moderate earthquake may topple shoring; with isolators installed but the moat unfinished, the building can strike temporary earth retention and suffer damage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"為每個施工階段建立模型，檢查在選定的施工期地震下，臨時支撐、已切柱位與未完成區的側向強度與變形；施工中每週更新已完成與未完成的柱位圖，確認實際進度沒有超出分析過的暫態組合。","textEn":"Model each construction stage and check the lateral strength and deformation of shoring, cut-column locations and unfinished zones under the selected construction-period earthquake; update a weekly plan of completed and pending column positions to confirm that actual progress stays within the analysed temporary states.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"合約應規定施工期地震的設計水準、同時施作範圍上限與緊急應變程序，地震後先由結構技師檢查臨時系統才可復工；進度變更須先送設計者評估暫態安全。","textEn":"The contract should set the construction-period design earthquake, the maximum simultaneous work area and an emergency procedure, with work resuming after an earthquake only once the structural engineer has inspected the temporary system; any change in sequence must first go to the designer for temporary-state assessment.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「施工期間的暫態結構與地震風險」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Temporary structural states and earthquake risk during construction\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","隔震支承的勁度與阻尼是固定值，不隨位移改變。","為每個施工階段建立模型，檢查在選定的施工期地震下，臨時支撐、已切柱位與未完成區的側向強度與變形。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","An isolator's stiffness and damping are fixed values that do not change with displacement.","Model each construction stage and check the lateral strength and deformation of shoring, cut-column locations and unfinished zones under the selected construction-period earthquake."],"answer":2,"explanation":"為每個施工階段建立模型，檢查在選定的施工期地震下，臨時支撐、已切柱位與未完成區的側向強度與變形；施工中每週更新已完成與未完成的柱位圖，確認實際進度沒有超出分析過的暫態組合。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Model each construction stage and check the lateral strength and deformation of shoring, cut-column locations and unfinished zones under the selected construction-period earthquake; update a weekly plan of completed and pending column positions to confirm that actual progress stays within the analysed temporary states. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b077-v13-24","title":"施工期間的暫態結構與地震風險：失效診斷","titleEn":"Temporary structural states and earthquake risk during construction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「施工期間地震風險」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Construction-period earthquake risk” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若施工單位為趕工而同時切斷超出計畫的柱數，結構進入沒有分析過的暫態，中度地震就可能使臨時支撐傾倒；隔震器已安裝但尚未完成隔震縫時，建築撞上開挖面的臨時擋土，也可能造成損傷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If the contractor cuts more columns than planned to save time, the structure enters an unanalysed temporary state in which a moderate earthquake may topple shoring; with isolators installed but the moat unfinished, the building can strike temporary earth retention and suffer damage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：設計者必須把每個施工階段當成一個暫態結構，決定其要承受的地震水準，並以臨時側向束制、限制同時施工範圍或分區施作來控制風險。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Designers must treat each construction stage as a temporary structure, choose the earthquake level it must resist, and control risk with temporary lateral restraints, limits on simultaneous work areas or zoned construction.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「施工期間只有幾年，不需要考慮地震。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Construction lasts only a few years, so earthquakes need not be considered.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若施工單位為趕工而同時切斷超出計畫的柱數，結構進入沒有分析過的暫態，中度地震就可能使臨時支撐傾倒；隔震器已安裝但尚未完成隔震縫時，建築撞上開挖面的臨時擋土，也可能造成損傷。","textEn":"If the contractor cuts more columns than planned to save time, the structure enters an unanalysed temporary state in which a moderate earthquake may topple shoring; with isolators installed but the moat unfinished, the building can strike temporary earth retention and suffer damage.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「施工期間的暫態結構與地震風險」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Temporary structural states and earthquake risk during construction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若施工單位為趕工而同時切斷超出計畫的柱數，結構進入沒有分析過的暫態，中度地震就可能使臨時支撐傾倒。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","隔震器只要在慢速試驗中合格，地震時的性質就一定相同。"],"optionsEn":["If the contractor cuts more columns than planned to save time, the structure enters an unanalysed temporary state in which a moderate earthquake may topple shoring.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","If an isolator passes slow-speed tests, its properties in an earthquake will be the same."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若施工單位為趕工而同時切斷超出計畫的柱數，結構進入沒有分析過的暫態，中度地震就可能使臨時支撐傾倒；隔震器已安裝但尚未完成隔震縫時，建築撞上開挖面的臨時擋土，也可能造成損傷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If the contractor cuts more columns than planned to save time, the structure enters an unanalysed temporary state in which a moderate earthquake may topple shoring; with isolators installed but the moat unfinished, the building can strike temporary earth retention and suffer damage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b077-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「原型試驗、出廠試驗與試驗設施」與「強震監測與實際性能判讀」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Prototype tests, production tests and test facilities\" and \"Strong-motion monitoring and interpreting real performance\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b077-v13-25","title":"原型試驗、出廠試驗與試驗設施：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Prototype tests, production tests and test facilities: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「隔震器試驗機」如何影響既有建築基礎隔震改造的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Isolator test machine” governs force, deformation or durability in “Base-isolation retrofit of existing buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"隔震器的性質必須在接近實際的軸壓、速度與位移下試驗，因為鉛心在快速大位移下會發熱、特性強度下降，橡膠性質也受速度與溫度影響。原型試驗在多個位移與軸壓組合下做反覆加載，確認穩定性與耗能；出廠試驗則對每個支承做壓縮與壓剪試驗，確認與原型一致。台灣國家地震工程研究中心的雙軸向動態測試系統（BATS）是少數能同時施加高軸壓與快速水平運動的設備，常用於隔震元件試驗。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「隔震器試驗機」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Isolator properties must be tested under realistic axial load, velocity and displacement, because the lead core heats and loses characteristic strength in fast large cycles, and rubber properties depend on rate and temperature. Prototype tests apply repeated cycles at several displacement and axial-load combinations to confirm stability and dissipation; production tests apply compression and combined compression–shear to every bearing to confirm consistency with the prototype. The Bi-Axial Testing System (BATS) at Taiwan's National Center for Research on Earthquake Engineering is one of the few facilities able to apply high axial load with fast horizontal motion and is commonly used for isolator testing. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Isolator test machine” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：某支承在 ±0.40 m 循環量得 +690 kN 與 −660 kN，K_eff = (690+660)/(2×0.40) ≈ 1,688 kN/m，比設計 1,679 kN/m 高約 0.5%；迴圈面積 250 kJ，β_eff = 250/(2π×1,688×0.40²) ≈ 14.7%，比設計 16% 低，須確認是否在允收範圍。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A bearing cycled to ±0.40 m reads +690 kN and −660 kN, so K_eff = (690+660)/(2×0.40) ≈ 1,688 kN/m, about 0.5% above the design 1,679 kN/m; a loop area of 250 kJ gives β_eff = 250/(2π×1,688×0.40²) ≈ 14.7%, below the design 16%, which must be checked against the acceptance range.","failure":"常見誤解：「隔震器只要在慢速試驗中合格，地震時的性質就一定相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If an isolator passes slow-speed tests, its properties in an earthquake will be the same.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「隔震器試驗機」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Isolator test machine”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-25-k1","title":"原型試驗、出廠試驗與試驗設施","titleEn":"Prototype tests, production tests and test facilities","text":"隔震器的性質必須在接近實際的軸壓、速度與位移下試驗，因為鉛心在快速大位移下會發熱、特性強度下降，橡膠性質也受速度與溫度影響。原型試驗在多個位移與軸壓組合下做反覆加載，確認穩定性與耗能；出廠試驗則對每個支承做壓縮與壓剪試驗，確認與原型一致。","textEn":"Isolator properties must be tested under realistic axial load, velocity and displacement, because the lead core heats and loses characteristic strength in fast large cycles, and rubber properties depend on rate and temperature. Prototype tests apply repeated cycles at several displacement and axial-load combinations to confirm stability and dissipation; production tests apply compression and combined compression–shear to every bearing to confirm consistency with the prototype.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：隔震器只要在慢速試驗中合格，地震時的性質就一定相同。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If an isolator passes slow-speed tests, its properties in an earthquake will be the same. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「原型試驗、出廠試驗與試驗設施」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Prototype tests, production tests and test facilities\" is correct?","options":["隔震器只要在慢速試驗中合格，地震時的性質就一定相同。","隔震器的性質必須在接近實際的軸壓、速度與位移下試驗，因為鉛心在快速大位移下會發熱、特性強度下降，橡膠性質也受速度與溫度影響。","小地震時隔震建築的加速度折減應該和設計地震一樣大。"],"optionsEn":["If an isolator passes slow-speed tests, its properties in an earthquake will be the same.","Isolator properties must be tested under realistic axial load, velocity and displacement, because the lead core heats and loses characteristic strength in fast large cycles, and rubber properties depend on rate and temperature.","In a small earthquake an isolated building should show the same acceleration reduction as in the design earthquake."],"answer":1,"explanation":"隔震器的性質必須在接近實際的軸壓、速度與位移下試驗，因為鉛心在快速大位移下會發熱、特性強度下降，橡膠性質也受速度與溫度影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Isolator properties must be tested under realistic axial load, velocity and displacement, because the lead core heats and loses characteristic strength in fast large cycles, and rubber properties depend on rate and temperature. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b077-v13-26","title":"原型試驗、出廠試驗與試驗設施：定量估算","titleEn":"Prototype tests, production tests and test facilities: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「隔震器試驗機」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Isolator test machine” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：某支承在 ±0.40 m 循環量得 +690 kN 與 −660 kN，K_eff = (690+660)/(2×0.40) ≈ 1,688 kN/m，比設計 1,679 kN/m 高約 0.5%；迴圈面積 250 kJ，β_eff = 250/(2π×1,688×0.40²) ≈ 14.7%，比設計 16% 低，須確認是否在允收範圍。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A bearing cycled to ±0.40 m reads +690 kN and −660 kN, so K_eff = (690+660)/(2×0.40) ≈ 1,688 kN/m, about 0.5% above the design 1,679 kN/m; a loop area of 250 kJ gives β_eff = 250/(2π×1,688×0.40²) ≈ 14.7%, below the design 16%, which must be checked against the acceptance range. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：試驗計畫列出軸壓、位移振幅、循環數、速度與溫度，以及 K_eff、EDC 個別與平均的允收偏差；試驗機的力量測方式要經校正，高速試驗時須考慮致動器慣性與摩擦對量測力的影響，並由第三方見證。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The test plan lists axial loads, displacement amplitudes, cycle counts, velocities and temperatures, and acceptance tolerances for individual and average K_eff and EDC; force measurement on the test machine must be calibrated, high-speed tests must account for actuator inertia and friction in the measured force, and a third party should witness.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"某支承在 ±0.40 m 循環量得 +690 kN 與 −660 kN，K_eff = (690+660)/(2×0.40) ≈ 1,688 kN/m，比設計 1,679 kN/m 高約 0.5%；迴圈面積 250 kJ，β_eff = 250/(2π×1,688×0.40²) ≈ 14.7%，比設計 16% 低，須確認是否在允收範圍。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A bearing cycled to ±0.40 m reads +690 kN and −660 kN, so K_eff = (690+660)/(2×0.40) ≈ 1,688 kN/m, about 0.5% above the design 1,679 kN/m; a loop area of 250 kJ gives β_eff = 250/(2π×1,688×0.40²) ≈ 14.7%, below the design 16%, which must be checked against the acceptance range. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「原型試驗、出廠試驗與試驗設施」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Prototype tests, production tests and test facilities\", which statement holds?","options":["隔震改造完成後，隔震縫只是一條空隙，不需要維護。","隔震縫寬度只要等於設計位移即可，不必考慮扭轉。","某支承在 ±0.40 m 循環量得 +690 kN 與 −660 kN，K_eff = (690+660)/(2×0.40) ≈ 1,688 kN/m，比設計 1,679 kN/m 高約 0.5%。"],"optionsEn":["Once the retrofit is complete, the moat is just a gap that needs no maintenance.","The moat width only needs to equal the design displacement, without considering torsion.","A bearing cycled to ±0.40 m reads +690 kN and −660 kN, so K_eff = (690+660)/(2×0.40) ≈ 1,688 kN/m, about 0.5% above the design 1,679 kN/m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"某支承在 ±0.40 m 循環量得 +690 kN 與 −660 kN，K_eff = (690+660)/(2×0.40) ≈ 1,688 kN/m，比設計 1,679 kN/m 高約 0.5%；迴圈面積 250 kJ，β_eff = 250/(2π×1,688×0.40²) ≈ 14.7%，比設計 16% 低，須確認是否在允收範圍。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A bearing cycled to ±0.40 m reads +690 kN and −660 kN, so K_eff = (690+660)/(2×0.40) ≈ 1,688 kN/m, about 0.5% above the design 1,679 kN/m; a loop area of 250 kJ gives β_eff = 250/(2π×1,688×0.40²) ≈ 14.7%, below the design 16%, which must be checked against the acceptance range. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b077-v13-27","title":"原型試驗、出廠試驗與試驗設施：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Prototype tests, production tests and test facilities: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「隔震器試驗機」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Isolator test machine” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"試驗計畫列出軸壓、位移振幅、循環數、速度與溫度，以及 K_eff、EDC 個別與平均的允收偏差；試驗機的力量測方式要經校正，高速試驗時須考慮致動器慣性與摩擦對量測力的影響，並由第三方見證。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The test plan lists axial loads, displacement amplitudes, cycle counts, velocities and temperatures, and acceptance tolerances for individual and average K_eff and EDC; force measurement on the test machine must be calibrated, high-speed tests must account for actuator inertia and friction in the measured force, and a third party should witness. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：採購文件要求原型試驗速度接近設計速度，或以經核可的方法換算速度效應；每個支承的試驗報告與序號要與安裝位置對照，不合格品不得以修正係數放行。","observationEn":"Site practice: Procurement documents should require prototype test velocities close to design velocity, or an approved method to account for rate effects; every bearing's test report and serial number must match its installed location, and failed units may not be released with correction factors.","failure":"注意干擾：若原型試驗只做慢速試驗，鉛心發熱造成的強度下降未被量到，分析高估了阻尼，實際位移超過隔震縫；出廠試驗若只抽樣，個別支承的黏結缺陷可能在地震中才暴露。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Slow-only prototype tests miss the strength loss from lead heating, so analysis overstates damping and real displacement exceeds the moat; sampling instead of testing every production bearing can leave individual bonding defects to reveal themselves in an earthquake. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"試驗計畫列出軸壓、位移振幅、循環數、速度與溫度，以及 K_eff、EDC 個別與平均的允收偏差；試驗機的力量測方式要經校正，高速試驗時須考慮致動器慣性與摩擦對量測力的影響，並由第三方見證。","textEn":"The test plan lists axial loads, displacement amplitudes, cycle counts, velocities and temperatures, and acceptance tolerances for individual and average K_eff and EDC; force measurement on the test machine must be calibrated, high-speed tests must account for actuator inertia and friction in the measured force, and a third party should witness.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"採購文件要求原型試驗速度接近設計速度，或以經核可的方法換算速度效應；每個支承的試驗報告與序號要與安裝位置對照，不合格品不得以修正係數放行。","textEn":"Procurement documents should require prototype test velocities close to design velocity, or an approved method to account for rate effects; every bearing's test report and serial number must match its installed location, and failed units may not be released with correction factors.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「原型試驗、出廠試驗與試驗設施」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Prototype tests, production tests and test facilities\"?","options":["試驗計畫列出軸壓、位移振幅、循環數、速度與溫度，以及 K_eff、EDC 個別與平均的允收偏差。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","新澆托換梁只要與舊柱接觸，就能自動把柱荷載傳過去。"],"optionsEn":["The test plan lists axial loads, displacement amplitudes, cycle counts, velocities and temperatures, and acceptance tolerances for individual and average K_eff and EDC.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A newly cast transfer beam that touches the old column will automatically pick up its load."],"answer":0,"explanation":"試驗計畫列出軸壓、位移振幅、循環數、速度與溫度，以及 K_eff、EDC 個別與平均的允收偏差；試驗機的力量測方式要經校正，高速試驗時須考慮致動器慣性與摩擦對量測力的影響，並由第三方見證。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The test plan lists axial loads, displacement amplitudes, cycle counts, velocities and temperatures, and acceptance tolerances for individual and average K_eff and EDC; force measurement on the test machine must be calibrated, high-speed tests must account for actuator inertia and friction in the measured force, and a third party should witness. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b077-v13-28","title":"原型試驗、出廠試驗與試驗設施：失效診斷","titleEn":"Prototype tests, production tests and test facilities: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「隔震器試驗機」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Isolator test machine” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若原型試驗只做慢速試驗，鉛心發熱造成的強度下降未被量到，分析高估了阻尼，實際位移超過隔震縫；出廠試驗若只抽樣，個別支承的黏結缺陷可能在地震中才暴露。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Slow-only prototype tests miss the strength loss from lead heating, so analysis overstates damping and real displacement exceeds the moat; sampling instead of testing every production bearing can leave individual bonding defects to reveal themselves in an earthquake. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：台灣國家地震工程研究中心的雙軸向動態測試系統（BATS）是少數能同時施加高軸壓與快速水平運動的設備，常用於隔震元件試驗。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The Bi-Axial Testing System (BATS) at Taiwan's National Center for Research on Earthquake Engineering is one of the few facilities able to apply high axial load with fast horizontal motion and is commonly used for isolator testing.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「隔震器只要在慢速試驗中合格，地震時的性質就一定相同。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If an isolator passes slow-speed tests, its properties in an earthquake will be the same.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若原型試驗只做慢速試驗，鉛心發熱造成的強度下降未被量到，分析高估了阻尼，實際位移超過隔震縫；出廠試驗若只抽樣，個別支承的黏結缺陷可能在地震中才暴露。","textEn":"Slow-only prototype tests miss the strength loss from lead heating, so analysis overstates damping and real displacement exceeds the moat; sampling instead of testing every production bearing can leave individual bonding defects to reveal themselves in an earthquake.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「原型試驗、出廠試驗與試驗設施」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Prototype tests, production tests and test facilities\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若原型試驗只做慢速試驗，鉛心發熱造成的強度下降未被量到，分析高估了阻尼，實際位移超過隔震縫；出廠試驗若只抽樣，個別支承的黏結缺陷可能在地震中才暴露。","小地震時隔震建築的加速度折減應該和設計地震一樣大。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Slow-only prototype tests miss the strength loss from lead heating, so analysis overstates damping and real displacement exceeds the moat.","In a small earthquake an isolated building should show the same acceleration reduction as in the design earthquake."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若原型試驗只做慢速試驗，鉛心發熱造成的強度下降未被量到，分析高估了阻尼，實際位移超過隔震縫；出廠試驗若只抽樣，個別支承的黏結缺陷可能在地震中才暴露。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Slow-only prototype tests miss the strength loss from lead heating, so analysis overstates damping and real displacement exceeds the moat; sampling instead of testing every production bearing can leave individual bonding defects to reveal themselves in an earthquake. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b077-v13-29","title":"強震監測與實際性能判讀：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Strong-motion monitoring and interpreting real performance: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「隔震層上下強震儀」如何影響既有建築基礎隔震改造的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Strong-motion sensors above and below isolation” governs force, deformation or durability in “Base-isolation retrofit of existing buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"隔震建築應在隔震層下方、上方與屋頂設置強震儀，並在隔震層設位移計，才能在地震後判斷隔震是否如預期作用。中小地震時鉛心可能未完全降伏，系統較硬、週期較短，加速度折減不如設計地震明顯，判讀時不能用設計週期直接比較。鹽湖城市郡大樓在 2020 年規模 5.7 地震後只需輕微修復，這類實際事件與紀錄是隔震改造最有說服力的驗證。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「隔震層上下強震儀」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An isolated building should carry strong-motion instruments below and above the isolation layer and at the roof, with displacement transducers in the isolation layer, so that engineers can judge after an earthquake whether isolation worked as intended. In small and moderate events the lead cores may not fully yield, so the system is stiffer with a shorter period and acceleration reduction is less marked than in the design earthquake; records must not be compared directly with the design period. After a magnitude 5.7 earthquake in 2020 the Salt Lake City and County Building needed only minor repairs, and such real events and records are the most convincing verification of an isolation retrofit. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Strong-motion sensors above and below isolation” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：隔震位移僅 0.03 m 時，單一支承 F = 177 + 1,237×0.03 ≈ 214 kN，K_eff ≈ 7,130 kN/m，54 個合計約 384,900 kN/m，T = 2π√(216,000/(9.81×384,900)) ≈ 1.5 s，只有設計位移 0.40 m 時 3.1 s 的一半。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: At only 0.03 m isolator displacement, one bearing carries F = 177 + 1,237×0.03 ≈ 214 kN, so K_eff ≈ 7,130 kN/m and 54 bearings total about 384,900 kN/m, giving T = 2π√(216,000/(9.81×384,900)) ≈ 1.5 s, half the 3.1 s at the 0.40 m design displacement.","failure":"常見誤解：「小地震時隔震建築的加速度折減應該和設計地震一樣大。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"In a small earthquake an isolated building should show the same acceleration reduction as in the design earthquake.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「隔震層上下強震儀」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Strong-motion sensors above and below isolation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-29-k1","title":"強震監測與實際性能判讀","titleEn":"Strong-motion monitoring and interpreting real performance","text":"隔震建築應在隔震層下方、上方與屋頂設置強震儀，並在隔震層設位移計，才能在地震後判斷隔震是否如預期作用。中小地震時鉛心可能未完全降伏，系統較硬、週期較短，加速度折減不如設計地震明顯，判讀時不能用設計週期直接比較。","textEn":"An isolated building should carry strong-motion instruments below and above the isolation layer and at the roof, with displacement transducers in the isolation layer, so that engineers can judge after an earthquake whether isolation worked as intended. In small and moderate events the lead cores may not fully yield, so the system is stiffer with a shorter period and acceleration reduction is less marked than in the design earthquake; records must not be compared directly with the design period.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：小地震時隔震建築的加速度折減應該和設計地震一樣大。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: In a small earthquake an isolated building should show the same acceleration reduction as in the design earthquake. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「強震監測與實際性能判讀」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Strong-motion monitoring and interpreting real performance\" is correct?","options":["小地震時隔震建築的加速度折減應該和設計地震一樣大。","只要用試驗量到的名目性質分析，隔震設計就涵蓋了全部情況。","隔震建築應在隔震層下方、上方與屋頂設置強震儀，並在隔震層設位移計，才能在地震後判斷隔震是否如預期作用。"],"optionsEn":["In a small earthquake an isolated building should show the same acceleration reduction as in the design earthquake.","Analysing with the nominal tested properties covers every case in isolation design.","An isolated building should carry strong-motion instruments below and above the isolation layer and at the roof, with displacement transducers in the isolation layer, so that engineers can judge after an earthquake whether isolation worked as intended."],"answer":2,"explanation":"隔震建築應在隔震層下方、上方與屋頂設置強震儀，並在隔震層設位移計，才能在地震後判斷隔震是否如預期作用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An isolated building should carry strong-motion instruments below and above the isolation layer and at the roof, with displacement transducers in the isolation layer, so that engineers can judge after an earthquake whether isolation worked as intended. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b077-v13-30","title":"強震監測與實際性能判讀：定量估算","titleEn":"Strong-motion monitoring and interpreting real performance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「隔震層上下強震儀」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Strong-motion sensors above and below isolation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：隔震位移僅 0.03 m 時，單一支承 F = 177 + 1,237×0.03 ≈ 214 kN，K_eff ≈ 7,130 kN/m，54 個合計約 384,900 kN/m，T = 2π√(216,000/(9.81×384,900)) ≈ 1.5 s，只有設計位移 0.40 m 時 3.1 s 的一半。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: At only 0.03 m isolator displacement, one bearing carries F = 177 + 1,237×0.03 ≈ 214 kN, so K_eff ≈ 7,130 kN/m and 54 bearings total about 384,900 kN/m, giving T = 2π√(216,000/(9.81×384,900)) ≈ 1.5 s, half the 3.1 s at the 0.40 m design displacement. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：地震後比較隔震層上下的尖峰加速度與傅立葉譜，計算傳遞比，並以位移計或刮痕板讀取最大位移；以紀錄反算的有效週期與阻尼，和相同位移下的雙線性模型預測比較，差異過大時檢查是否有障礙物阻擋或支承損傷。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After an earthquake, compare peak accelerations and Fourier spectra above and below the isolation layer to compute transfer ratios, and read maximum displacement from transducers or scratch plates; compare effective period and damping back-calculated from records with the bilinear model at the same displacement, and check for obstructions or bearing damage where they differ greatly.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"隔震位移僅 0.03 m 時，單一支承 F = 177 + 1,237×0.03 ≈ 214 kN，K_eff ≈ 7,130 kN/m，54 個合計約 384,900 kN/m，T = 2π√(216,000/(9.81×384,900)) ≈ 1.5 s，只有設計位移 0.40 m 時 3.1 s 的一半。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"At only 0.03 m isolator displacement, one bearing carries F = 177 + 1,237×0.03 ≈ 214 kN, so K_eff ≈ 7,130 kN/m and 54 bearings total about 384,900 kN/m, giving T = 2π√(216,000/(9.81×384,900)) ≈ 1.5 s, half the 3.1 s at the 0.40 m design displacement. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「強震監測與實際性能判讀」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Strong-motion monitoring and interpreting real performance\", which statement holds?","options":["隔震位移僅 0.03 m 時，單一支承 F = 177 + 1,237×0.03 ≈ 214 kN，K_eff ≈ 7,130 kN/m，54 個合計約 384,900 kN/m，T = 2π√(216,000/(9.81×384,900)) ≈ 1.5 s，只有設計位移 0.40 m 時 3.1 s 的一半。","隔震改造會讓建築在地震中完全不動。","隔震支承的勁度與阻尼是固定值，不隨位移改變。"],"optionsEn":["At only 0.03 m isolator displacement, one bearing carries F = 177 + 1,237×0.03 ≈ 214 kN, so K_eff ≈ 7,130 kN/m and 54 bearings total about 384,900 kN/m, giving T = 2π√(216,000/(9.81×384,900)) ≈ 1.5 s, half the 3.1 s at the 0.40 m design displacement.","Base isolation makes a building stay completely still in an earthquake.","An isolator's stiffness and damping are fixed values that do not change with displacement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"隔震位移僅 0.03 m 時，單一支承 F = 177 + 1,237×0.03 ≈ 214 kN，K_eff ≈ 7,130 kN/m，54 個合計約 384,900 kN/m，T = 2π√(216,000/(9.81×384,900)) ≈ 1.5 s，只有設計位移 0.40 m 時 3.1 s 的一半。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"At only 0.03 m isolator displacement, one bearing carries F = 177 + 1,237×0.03 ≈ 214 kN, so K_eff ≈ 7,130 kN/m and 54 bearings total about 384,900 kN/m, giving T = 2π√(216,000/(9.81×384,900)) ≈ 1.5 s, half the 3.1 s at the 0.40 m design displacement. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b077-v13-31","title":"強震監測與實際性能判讀：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Strong-motion monitoring and interpreting real performance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「隔震層上下強震儀」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Strong-motion sensors above and below isolation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"地震後比較隔震層上下的尖峰加速度與傅立葉譜，計算傳遞比，並以位移計或刮痕板讀取最大位移；以紀錄反算的有效週期與阻尼，和相同位移下的雙線性模型預測比較，差異過大時檢查是否有障礙物阻擋或支承損傷。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After an earthquake, compare peak accelerations and Fourier spectra above and below the isolation layer to compute transfer ratios, and read maximum displacement from transducers or scratch plates; compare effective period and damping back-calculated from records with the bilinear model at the same displacement, and check for obstructions or bearing damage where they differ greatly. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：業主應編列強震儀維護與資料判讀預算，地震後在約定時間內由結構技師提出簡報，說明最大位移、傳遞比與是否需要檢查支承；紀錄長期保存供後續研究與再評估。","observationEn":"Site practice: Owners should budget for instrument maintenance and data interpretation, with the structural engineer reporting within an agreed time after each earthquake on maximum displacement, transfer ratios and whether bearings need inspection; keep records permanently for research and reassessment.","failure":"注意干擾：若沒有隔震層下方的強震儀，就無法區分加速度降低是因為隔震還是地動本身較弱；若隔震縫被雜物或後來增建的構造卡住，紀錄會顯示上部加速度突然尖峰，代表發生撞擊。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Without an instrument below the isolation layer, nobody can tell whether lower acceleration came from isolation or simply weaker ground motion; if debris or later construction blocks the moat, records show sudden acceleration spikes above the layer, the signature of impact. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"地震後比較隔震層上下的尖峰加速度與傅立葉譜，計算傳遞比，並以位移計或刮痕板讀取最大位移；以紀錄反算的有效週期與阻尼，和相同位移下的雙線性模型預測比較，差異過大時檢查是否有障礙物阻擋或支承損傷。","textEn":"After an earthquake, compare peak accelerations and Fourier spectra above and below the isolation layer to compute transfer ratios, and read maximum displacement from transducers or scratch plates; compare effective period and damping back-calculated from records with the bilinear model at the same displacement, and check for obstructions or bearing damage where they differ greatly.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"業主應編列強震儀維護與資料判讀預算，地震後在約定時間內由結構技師提出簡報，說明最大位移、傳遞比與是否需要檢查支承；紀錄長期保存供後續研究與再評估。","textEn":"Owners should budget for instrument maintenance and data interpretation, with the structural engineer reporting within an agreed time after each earthquake on maximum displacement, transfer ratios and whether bearings need inspection; keep records permanently for research and reassessment.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「強震監測與實際性能判讀」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Strong-motion monitoring and interpreting real performance\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","地震後比較隔震層上下的尖峰加速度與傅立葉譜，計算傳遞比，並以位移計或刮痕板讀取最大位移。","切柱只是施工手續，只要千斤頂撐住就不會影響上部結構。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","After an earthquake, compare peak accelerations and Fourier spectra above and below the isolation layer to compute transfer ratios, and read maximum displacement from transducers or scratch plates.","Cutting columns is a routine step; as long as jacks hold them, the superstructure is unaffected."],"answer":1,"explanation":"地震後比較隔震層上下的尖峰加速度與傅立葉譜，計算傳遞比，並以位移計或刮痕板讀取最大位移；以紀錄反算的有效週期與阻尼，和相同位移下的雙線性模型預測比較，差異過大時檢查是否有障礙物阻擋或支承損傷。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After an earthquake, compare peak accelerations and Fourier spectra above and below the isolation layer to compute transfer ratios, and read maximum displacement from transducers or scratch plates; compare effective period and damping back-calculated from records with the bilinear model at the same displacement, and check for obstructions or bearing damage where they differ greatly. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b077-v13-32","title":"強震監測與實際性能判讀：失效診斷","titleEn":"Strong-motion monitoring and interpreting real performance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「隔震層上下強震儀」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Strong-motion sensors above and below isolation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若沒有隔震層下方的強震儀，就無法區分加速度降低是因為隔震還是地動本身較弱；若隔震縫被雜物或後來增建的構造卡住，紀錄會顯示上部加速度突然尖峰，代表發生撞擊。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Without an instrument below the isolation layer, nobody can tell whether lower acceleration came from isolation or simply weaker ground motion; if debris or later construction blocks the moat, records show sudden acceleration spikes above the layer, the signature of impact. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：鹽湖城市郡大樓在 2020 年規模 5.7 地震後只需輕微修復，這類實際事件與紀錄是隔震改造最有說服力的驗證。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: After a magnitude 5.7 earthquake in 2020 the Salt Lake City and County Building needed only minor repairs, and such real events and records are the most convincing verification of an isolation retrofit.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「小地震時隔震建築的加速度折減應該和設計地震一樣大。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"In a small earthquake an isolated building should show the same acceleration reduction as in the design earthquake.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若沒有隔震層下方的強震儀，就無法區分加速度降低是因為隔震還是地動本身較弱；若隔震縫被雜物或後來增建的構造卡住，紀錄會顯示上部加速度突然尖峰，代表發生撞擊。","textEn":"Without an instrument below the isolation layer, nobody can tell whether lower acceleration came from isolation or simply weaker ground motion; if debris or later construction blocks the moat, records show sudden acceleration spikes above the layer, the signature of impact.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「強震監測與實際性能判讀」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Strong-motion monitoring and interpreting real performance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要用試驗量到的名目性質分析，隔震設計就涵蓋了全部情況。","若沒有隔震層下方的強震儀，就無法區分加速度降低是因為隔震還是地動本身較弱；若隔震縫被雜物或後來增建的構造卡住，紀錄會顯示上部加速度突然尖峰，代表發生撞擊。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Analysing with the nominal tested properties covers every case in isolation design.","Without an instrument below the isolation layer, nobody can tell whether lower acceleration came from isolation or simply weaker ground motion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若沒有隔震層下方的強震儀，就無法區分加速度降低是因為隔震還是地動本身較弱；若隔震縫被雜物或後來增建的構造卡住，紀錄會顯示上部加速度突然尖峰，代表發生撞擊。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Without an instrument below the isolation layer, nobody can tell whether lower acceleration came from isolation or simply weaker ground motion; if debris or later construction blocks the moat, records show sudden acceleration spikes above the layer, the signature of impact. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b077-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「老化、溫度與性質上下限分析」與「隔震縫維護、事件後檢查與交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ageing, temperature and upper- and lower-bound analysis\" and \"Moat maintenance, post-event inspection and handover\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b077-v13-33","title":"老化、溫度與性質上下限分析：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Ageing, temperature and upper- and lower-bound analysis: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「性質修正係數」如何影響既有建築基礎隔震改造的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Property modification factors” governs force, deformation or durability in “Base-isolation retrofit of existing buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"隔震器的性質不是固定值：橡膠會隨時間硬化、低溫時變硬，鉛心在連續大位移中發熱而強度下降，製造批次也有變異。因此設計不採用單一性質，而以性質修正係數產生上限與下限兩組性質分別分析：下限性質（較軟、阻尼較低）決定最大位移與隔震縫寬度，上限性質（較硬、強度較高）決定上部結構與托換構件的設計力。改造案的上部結構往往只有有限的強度，對上限力特別敏感。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「性質修正係數」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Isolator properties are not fixed: rubber stiffens with age and at low temperature, lead cores heat and lose strength in repeated large cycles, and production batches vary. Design therefore uses property modification factors to create upper- and lower-bound property sets analysed separately: the lower bound, softer with less damping, governs maximum displacement and moat width, while the upper bound, stiffer and stronger, governs forces on the superstructure and transfer members. In a retrofit the superstructure often has limited strength and is especially sensitive to upper-bound forces. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Property modification factors” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：上限取 Q_d×1.3、K_d×1.1：F_up = 1.3×177 + 1.1×1,237×0.40 ≈ 774 kN，為名目 672 kN 的 1.15 倍；下限取 Q_d×0.85、K_d×0.9：F_lo = 0.85×177 + 0.9×1,237×0.40 ≈ 596 kN，系統週期由 3.1 s 增為約 3.3 s，位移需求隨之增加。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Upper bound with Q_d×1.3 and K_d×1.1: F_up = 1.3×177 + 1.1×1,237×0.40 ≈ 774 kN, 1.15 times the nominal 672 kN; lower bound with Q_d×0.85 and K_d×0.9: F_lo = 0.85×177 + 0.9×1,237×0.40 ≈ 596 kN, lengthening the system period from 3.1 s to about 3.3 s and raising displacement demand.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要用試驗量到的名目性質分析，隔震設計就涵蓋了全部情況。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Analysing with the nominal tested properties covers every case in isolation design.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「性質修正係數」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Property modification factors”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-33-k1","title":"老化、溫度與性質上下限分析","titleEn":"Ageing, temperature and upper- and lower-bound analysis","text":"隔震器的性質不是固定值：橡膠會隨時間硬化、低溫時變硬，鉛心在連續大位移中發熱而強度下降，製造批次也有變異。因此設計不採用單一性質，而以性質修正係數產生上限與下限兩組性質分別分析：下限性質（較軟、阻尼較低）決定最大位移與隔震縫寬度，上限性質（較硬、強度較高）決定上部結構與托換構件的設計力。","textEn":"Isolator properties are not fixed: rubber stiffens with age and at low temperature, lead cores heat and lose strength in repeated large cycles, and production batches vary. Design therefore uses property modification factors to create upper- and lower-bound property sets analysed separately: the lower bound, softer with less damping, governs maximum displacement and moat width, while the upper bound, stiffer and stronger, governs forces on the superstructure and transfer members.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要用試驗量到的名目性質分析，隔震設計就涵蓋了全部情況。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Analysing with the nominal tested properties covers every case in isolation design. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「老化、溫度與性質上下限分析」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ageing, temperature and upper- and lower-bound analysis\" is correct?","options":["隔震器的性質不是固定值：橡膠會隨時間硬化、低溫時變硬，鉛心在連續大位移中發熱而強度下降，製造批次也有變異。","只要用試驗量到的名目性質分析，隔震設計就涵蓋了全部情況。","隔震改造完成後，隔震縫只是一條空隙，不需要維護。"],"optionsEn":["Isolator properties are not fixed: rubber stiffens with age and at low temperature, lead cores heat and lose strength in repeated large cycles, and production batches vary.","Analysing with the nominal tested properties covers every case in isolation design.","Once the retrofit is complete, the moat is just a gap that needs no maintenance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"隔震器的性質不是固定值：橡膠會隨時間硬化、低溫時變硬，鉛心在連續大位移中發熱而強度下降，製造批次也有變異。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Isolator properties are not fixed: rubber stiffens with age and at low temperature, lead cores heat and lose strength in repeated large cycles, and production batches vary. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b077-v13-34","title":"老化、溫度與性質上下限分析：定量估算","titleEn":"Ageing, temperature and upper- and lower-bound analysis: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「性質修正係數」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Property modification factors” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：上限取 Q_d×1.3、K_d×1.1：F_up = 1.3×177 + 1.1×1,237×0.40 ≈ 774 kN，為名目 672 kN 的 1.15 倍；下限取 Q_d×0.85、K_d×0.9：F_lo = 0.85×177 + 0.9×1,237×0.40 ≈ 596 kN，系統週期由 3.1 s 增為約 3.3 s，位移需求隨之增加。修正係數為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Upper bound with Q_d×1.3 and K_d×1.1: F_up = 1.3×177 + 1.1×1,237×0.40 ≈ 774 kN, 1.15 times the nominal 672 kN; lower bound with Q_d×0.85 and K_d×0.9: F_lo = 0.85×177 + 0.9×1,237×0.40 ≈ 596 kN, lengthening the system period from 3.1 s to about 3.3 s and raising displacement demand. The factors are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：性質修正係數須以製造商的老化、溫度、速度與循環試驗資料為依據；設計報告同時列出上下限分析的最大位移、基底剪力與上部結構需求比，並在維護計畫中規定定期抽檢或量測支承變形與外觀。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Property modification factors must rest on the manufacturer's ageing, temperature, rate and cycling test data; the design report lists maximum displacement, base shear and superstructure demand ratios for both bounds, and the maintenance plan requires periodic inspection of bearing deformation and condition.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"上限取 Q_d×1.3、K_d×1.1：F_up = 1.3×177 + 1.1×1,237×0.40 ≈ 774 kN，為名目 672 kN 的 1.15 倍；下限取 Q_d×0.85、K_d×0.9：F_lo = 0.85×177 + 0.9×1,237×0.40 ≈ 596 kN，系統週期由 3.1 s 增為約 3.3 s，位移需求隨之增加。修正係數為教學假設。","textEn":"Upper bound with Q_d×1.3 and K_d×1.1: F_up = 1.3×177 + 1.1×1,237×0.40 ≈ 774 kN, 1.15 times the nominal 672 kN; lower bound with Q_d×0.85 and K_d×0.9: F_lo = 0.85×177 + 0.9×1,237×0.40 ≈ 596 kN, lengthening the system period from 3.1 s to about 3.3 s and raising displacement demand. The factors are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「老化、溫度與性質上下限分析」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ageing, temperature and upper- and lower-bound analysis\", which statement holds?","options":["隔震縫寬度只要等於設計位移即可，不必考慮扭轉。","上限取 Q_d×1.3、K_d×1.1：F_up = 1.3×177 + 1.1×1,237×0.40 ≈ 774 kN，為名目 672 kN 的 1.15 倍。","新澆托換梁只要與舊柱接觸，就能自動把柱荷載傳過去。"],"optionsEn":["The moat width only needs to equal the design displacement, without considering torsion.","Upper bound with Q_d×1.3 and K_d×1.1: F_up = 1.3×177 + 1.1×1,237×0.40 ≈ 774 kN, 1.15 times the nominal 672 kN.","A newly cast transfer beam that touches the old column will automatically pick up its load."],"answer":1,"explanation":"上限取 Q_d×1.3、K_d×1.1：F_up = 1.3×177 + 1.1×1,237×0.40 ≈ 774 kN，為名目 672 kN 的 1.15 倍；下限取 Q_d×0.85、K_d×0.9：F_lo = 0.85×177 + 0.9×1,237×0.40 ≈ 596 kN，系統週期由 3.1 s 增為約 3.3 s，位移需求隨之增加。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Upper bound with Q_d×1.3 and K_d×1.1: F_up = 1.3×177 + 1.1×1,237×0.40 ≈ 774 kN, 1.15 times the nominal 672 kN; lower bound with Q_d×0.85 and K_d×0.9: F_lo = 0.85×177 + 0.9×1,237×0.40 ≈ 596 kN, lengthening the system period from 3.1 s to about 3.3 s and raising displacement demand. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b077-v13-35","title":"老化、溫度與性質上下限分析：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ageing, temperature and upper- and lower-bound analysis: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「性質修正係數」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Property modification factors” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"性質修正係數須以製造商的老化、溫度、速度與循環試驗資料為依據；設計報告同時列出上下限分析的最大位移、基底剪力與上部結構需求比，並在維護計畫中規定定期抽檢或量測支承變形與外觀。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Property modification factors must rest on the manufacturer's ageing, temperature, rate and cycling test data; the design report lists maximum displacement, base shear and superstructure demand ratios for both bounds, and the maintenance plan requires periodic inspection of bearing deformation and condition. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接文件中列出每種支承的名目、上限與下限性質及其依據，任何更換支承都必須落在同一上下限範圍內；外觀檢查項目包括橡膠龜裂、鋼板外露鏽蝕、殘留側向變形與錨栓。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover documents list nominal, upper- and lower-bound properties and their basis for each bearing type, and any replacement bearing must fall within the same bounds; visual inspection covers rubber cracking, exposed or corroded shims, residual lateral offset and anchor bolts.","failure":"注意干擾：若只以名目性質分析，橡膠多年硬化後實際傳入上部結構的力比設計高一至兩成，脆弱的磚牆或石材裝飾可能在設計地震中受損；低溫地區若忽略橡膠硬化，冬季地震的隔震效果也會打折。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Analysing only nominal properties means that after years of rubber stiffening the forces reaching the superstructure are 10% to 20% above design, so brittle masonry or stone ornament can be damaged in the design earthquake; ignoring low-temperature stiffening in cold climates also reduces isolation in a winter earthquake. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"性質修正係數須以製造商的老化、溫度、速度與循環試驗資料為依據；設計報告同時列出上下限分析的最大位移、基底剪力與上部結構需求比，並在維護計畫中規定定期抽檢或量測支承變形與外觀。","textEn":"Property modification factors must rest on the manufacturer's ageing, temperature, rate and cycling test data; the design report lists maximum displacement, base shear and superstructure demand ratios for both bounds, and the maintenance plan requires periodic inspection of bearing deformation and condition.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接文件中列出每種支承的名目、上限與下限性質及其依據，任何更換支承都必須落在同一上下限範圍內；外觀檢查項目包括橡膠龜裂、鋼板外露鏽蝕、殘留側向變形與錨栓。","textEn":"Handover documents list nominal, upper- and lower-bound properties and their basis for each bearing type, and any replacement bearing must fall within the same bounds; visual inspection covers rubber cracking, exposed or corroded shims, residual lateral offset and anchor bolts.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「老化、溫度與性質上下限分析」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ageing, temperature and upper- and lower-bound analysis\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","施工期間只有幾年，不需要考慮地震。","性質修正係數須以製造商的老化、溫度、速度與循環試驗資料為依據。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Construction lasts only a few years, so earthquakes need not be considered.","Property modification factors must rest on the manufacturer's ageing, temperature, rate and cycling test data."],"answer":2,"explanation":"性質修正係數須以製造商的老化、溫度、速度與循環試驗資料為依據；設計報告同時列出上下限分析的最大位移、基底剪力與上部結構需求比，並在維護計畫中規定定期抽檢或量測支承變形與外觀。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Property modification factors must rest on the manufacturer's ageing, temperature, rate and cycling test data; the design report lists maximum displacement, base shear and superstructure demand ratios for both bounds, and the maintenance plan requires periodic inspection of bearing deformation and condition. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b077-v13-36","title":"老化、溫度與性質上下限分析：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ageing, temperature and upper- and lower-bound analysis: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「性質修正係數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Property modification factors” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只以名目性質分析，橡膠多年硬化後實際傳入上部結構的力比設計高一至兩成，脆弱的磚牆或石材裝飾可能在設計地震中受損；低溫地區若忽略橡膠硬化，冬季地震的隔震效果也會打折。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Analysing only nominal properties means that after years of rubber stiffening the forces reaching the superstructure are 10% to 20% above design, so brittle masonry or stone ornament can be damaged in the design earthquake; ignoring low-temperature stiffening in cold climates also reduces isolation in a winter earthquake. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：改造案的上部結構往往只有有限的強度，對上限力特別敏感。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: In a retrofit the superstructure often has limited strength and is especially sensitive to upper-bound forces.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要用試驗量到的名目性質分析，隔震設計就涵蓋了全部情況。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Analysing with the nominal tested properties covers every case in isolation design.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只以名目性質分析，橡膠多年硬化後實際傳入上部結構的力比設計高一至兩成，脆弱的磚牆或石材裝飾可能在設計地震中受損；低溫地區若忽略橡膠硬化，冬季地震的隔震效果也會打折。","textEn":"Analysing only nominal properties means that after years of rubber stiffening the forces reaching the superstructure are 10% to 20% above design, so brittle masonry or stone ornament can be damaged in the design earthquake; ignoring low-temperature stiffening in cold climates also reduces isolation in a winter earthquake.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「老化、溫度與性質上下限分析」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ageing, temperature and upper- and lower-bound analysis\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若只以名目性質分析，橡膠多年硬化後實際傳入上部結構的力比設計高一至兩成，脆弱的磚牆或石材裝飾可能在設計地震中受損。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","隔震改造完成後，隔震縫只是一條空隙，不需要維護。"],"optionsEn":["Analysing only nominal properties means that after years of rubber stiffening the forces reaching the superstructure are 10% to 20% above design, so brittle masonry or stone ornament can be damaged in the design earthquake.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Once the retrofit is complete, the moat is just a gap that needs no maintenance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若只以名目性質分析，橡膠多年硬化後實際傳入上部結構的力比設計高一至兩成，脆弱的磚牆或石材裝飾可能在設計地震中受損；低溫地區若忽略橡膠硬化，冬季地震的隔震效果也會打折。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Analysing only nominal properties means that after years of rubber stiffening the forces reaching the superstructure are 10% to 20% above design, so brittle masonry or stone ornament can be damaged in the design earthquake; ignoring low-temperature stiffening in cold climates also reduces isolation in a winter earthquake. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b077-v13-37","title":"隔震縫維護、事件後檢查與交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Moat maintenance, post-event inspection and handover: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「隔震縫淨空與管線接頭」如何影響既有建築基礎隔震改造的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Moat clearance and utility joints” governs force, deformation or durability in “Base-isolation retrofit of existing buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"隔震改造完成後，最常見的失效不是支承本身，而是隔震縫被逐漸填滿：新增的花台、儲藏物、管線支架、甚至修繕時加砌的牆，都可能在多年後把建築與地盤重新卡在一起。穿越隔震面的水管、瓦斯管、電纜與排水管也必須保留足夠的可動長度。因此交接文件與日常維護必須把隔震縫當成結構構件管理，並在每次地震後檢查支承、可動接頭與隔震縫是否完整。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「隔震縫淨空與管線接頭」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After an isolation retrofit, the most common failure is not the bearings but the moat gradually filling up: new planters, storage, pipe supports or even walls added during repairs can lock the building to the ground again years later. Water, gas, power and drainage lines crossing the isolation plane must also keep enough movable length. Handover documents and routine maintenance must therefore manage the moat as a structural element, and after every earthquake inspect bearings, flexible joints and moat clearance. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Moat clearance and utility joints” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：若隔震縫被後來的構造縮減到 0.30 m，而設計位移為 0.40 m：系統質量約 216,000/9.81 ≈ 22,000 t，ω = 2π/3.1 ≈ 2.03 rad/s，在 0.30 m 處速度 v = ω·√(0.40² − 0.30²) ≈ 0.54 m/s，撞擊動能 ½mv² ≈ 0.5×22.0×10⁶×0.54² ≈ 3.2 MJ，全部傳入局部牆體與上部結構。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: If later construction reduces the moat to 0.30 m while the design displacement is 0.40 m: the system mass is about 216,000/9.81 ≈ 22,000 t, ω = 2π/3.1 ≈ 2.03 rad/s, the velocity at 0.30 m is v = ω·√(0.40² − 0.30²) ≈ 0.54 m/s and the impact energy ½mv² ≈ 0.5×22.0×10⁶×0.54² ≈ 3.2 MJ, all delivered into local walls and the superstructure.","failure":"常見誤解：「隔震改造完成後，隔震縫只是一條空隙，不需要維護。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once the retrofit is complete, the moat is just a gap that needs no maintenance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「隔震縫淨空與管線接頭」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Moat clearance and utility joints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-37-k1","title":"隔震縫維護、事件後檢查與交接","titleEn":"Moat maintenance, post-event inspection and handover","text":"隔震改造完成後，最常見的失效不是支承本身，而是隔震縫被逐漸填滿：新增的花台、儲藏物、管線支架、甚至修繕時加砌的牆，都可能在多年後把建築與地盤重新卡在一起。穿越隔震面的水管、瓦斯管、電纜與排水管也必須保留足夠的可動長度。","textEn":"After an isolation retrofit, the most common failure is not the bearings but the moat gradually filling up: new planters, storage, pipe supports or even walls added during repairs can lock the building to the ground again years later. Water, gas, power and drainage lines crossing the isolation plane must also keep enough movable length.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：隔震改造完成後，隔震縫只是一條空隙，不需要維護。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once the retrofit is complete, the moat is just a gap that needs no maintenance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「隔震縫維護、事件後檢查與交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Moat maintenance, post-event inspection and handover\" is correct?","options":["隔震改造完成後，隔震縫只是一條空隙，不需要維護。","隔震改造完成後，最常見的失效不是支承本身，而是隔震縫被逐漸填滿：新增的花台、儲藏物、管線支架、甚至修繕時加砌的牆，都可能在多年後把建築與地盤重新卡在一起。","隔震改造會讓建築在地震中完全不動。"],"optionsEn":["Once the retrofit is complete, the moat is just a gap that needs no maintenance.","After an isolation retrofit, the most common failure is not the bearings but the moat gradually filling up: new planters, storage, pipe supports or even walls added during repairs can lock the building to the ground again years later.","Base isolation makes a building stay completely still in an earthquake."],"answer":1,"explanation":"隔震改造完成後，最常見的失效不是支承本身，而是隔震縫被逐漸填滿：新增的花台、儲藏物、管線支架、甚至修繕時加砌的牆，都可能在多年後把建築與地盤重新卡在一起。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After an isolation retrofit, the most common failure is not the bearings but the moat gradually filling up: new planters, storage, pipe supports or even walls added during repairs can lock the building to the ground again years later. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b077-v13-38","title":"隔震縫維護、事件後檢查與交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Moat maintenance, post-event inspection and handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「隔震縫淨空與管線接頭」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Moat clearance and utility joints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：若隔震縫被後來的構造縮減到 0.30 m，而設計位移為 0.40 m：系統質量約 216,000/9.81 ≈ 22,000 t，ω = 2π/3.1 ≈ 2.03 rad/s，在 0.30 m 處速度 v = ω·√(0.40² − 0.30²) ≈ 0.54 m/s，撞擊動能 ½mv² ≈ 0.5×22.0×10⁶×0.54² ≈ 3.2 MJ，全部傳入局部牆體與上部結構。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: If later construction reduces the moat to 0.30 m while the design displacement is 0.40 m: the system mass is about 216,000/9.81 ≈ 22,000 t, ω = 2π/3.1 ≈ 2.03 rad/s, the velocity at 0.30 m is v = ω·√(0.40² − 0.30²) ≈ 0.54 m/s and the impact energy ½mv² ≈ 0.5×22.0×10⁶×0.54² ≈ 3.2 MJ, all delivered into local walls and the superstructure. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每年沿隔震縫全周量測淨寬並拍照，檢查蓋板、伸縮踏板與管線可動接頭；地震後依檢查表記錄支承殘留變形、橡膠龜裂、鉛心外露、錨栓與刮痕板讀數，必要時抽樣更換支承並重新試驗。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Each year measure and photograph the clear width all round the moat and inspect covers, sliding treads and flexible utility joints; after an earthquake record residual bearing offset, rubber cracking, lead exposure, anchor bolts and scratch-plate readings against a checklist, replacing and re-testing sample bearings where needed.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"若隔震縫被後來的構造縮減到 0.30 m，而設計位移為 0.40 m：系統質量約 216,000/9.81 ≈ 22,000 t，ω = 2π/3.1 ≈ 2.03 rad/s，在 0.30 m 處速度 v = ω·√(0.40² − 0.30²) ≈ 0.54 m/s，撞擊動能 ½mv² ≈ 0.5×22.0×10⁶×0.54² ≈ 3.2 MJ，全部傳入局部牆體與上部結構。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"If later construction reduces the moat to 0.30 m while the design displacement is 0.40 m: the system mass is about 216,000/9.81 ≈ 22,000 t, ω = 2π/3.1 ≈ 2.03 rad/s, the velocity at 0.30 m is v = ω·√(0.40² − 0.30²) ≈ 0.54 m/s and the impact energy ½mv² ≈ 0.5×22.0×10⁶×0.54² ≈ 3.2 MJ, all delivered into local walls and the superstructure. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「隔震縫維護、事件後檢查與交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Moat maintenance, post-event inspection and handover\", which statement holds?","options":["隔震支承的勁度與阻尼是固定值，不隨位移改變。","切柱只是施工手續，只要千斤頂撐住就不會影響上部結構。","若隔震縫被後來的構造縮減到 0.30 m，而設計位移為 0.40 m：系統質量約 216,000/9.81 ≈ 22,000 t，ω = 2π/3.1 ≈ 2.03 rad/s，在 0.30 m 處速度 v = ω·√(0.40² − 0.30²) ≈ 0.54 m/s，撞擊動能 ½mv² ≈ 0.5×22.0×10⁶×0.54² ≈ 3.2 MJ，全部傳入局部牆體與上部結構。"],"optionsEn":["An isolator's stiffness and damping are fixed values that do not change with displacement.","Cutting columns is a routine step; as long as jacks hold them, the superstructure is unaffected.","If later construction reduces the moat to 0.30 m while the design displacement is 0.40 m: the system mass is about 216,000/9.81 ≈ 22,000 t, ω = 2π/3.1 ≈ 2.03 rad/s, the velocity at 0.30 m is v = ω·√(0.40² − 0.30²) ≈ 0.54 m/s and the impact energy ½mv² ≈ 0.5×22.0×10⁶×0.54² ≈ 3.2 MJ, all delivered into local walls and the superstructure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若隔震縫被後來的構造縮減到 0.30 m，而設計位移為 0.40 m：系統質量約 216,000/9.81 ≈ 22,000 t，ω = 2π/3.1 ≈ 2.03 rad/s，在 0.30 m 處速度 v = ω·√(0.40² − 0.30²) ≈ 0.54 m/s，撞擊動能 ½mv² ≈ 0.5×22.0×10⁶×0.54² ≈ 3.2 MJ，全部傳入局部牆體與上部結構。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"If later construction reduces the moat to 0.30 m while the design displacement is 0.40 m: the system mass is about 216,000/9.81 ≈ 22,000 t, ω = 2π/3.1 ≈ 2.03 rad/s, the velocity at 0.30 m is v = ω·√(0.40² − 0.30²) ≈ 0.54 m/s and the impact energy ½mv² ≈ 0.5×22.0×10⁶×0.54² ≈ 3.2 MJ, all delivered into local walls and the superstructure. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b077-v13-39","title":"隔震縫維護、事件後檢查與交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Moat maintenance, post-event inspection and handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「隔震縫淨空與管線接頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Moat clearance and utility joints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每年沿隔震縫全周量測淨寬並拍照，檢查蓋板、伸縮踏板與管線可動接頭；地震後依檢查表記錄支承殘留變形、橡膠龜裂、鉛心外露、錨栓與刮痕板讀數，必要時抽樣更換支承並重新試驗。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Each year measure and photograph the clear width all round the moat and inspect covers, sliding treads and flexible utility joints; after an earthquake record residual bearing offset, rubber cracking, lead exposure, anchor bolts and scratch-plate readings against a checklist, replacing and re-testing sample bearings where needed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接文件應包含隔震設計基準、支承位置與性質表、上下限分析結果、隔震縫與可動接頭圖、檢查週期與事件後檢查表，並明訂任何在隔震縫範圍內的施作須先經結構技師核可。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover should include the isolation design basis, bearing location and property tables, bound-analysis results, plans of the moat and flexible joints, inspection intervals and the post-event checklist, and state that any work within the moat zone requires prior approval by the structural engineer.","failure":"注意干擾：管理單位不了解隔震縫的功能，把它當成可利用空間，或在外牆修繕時加設與地面相連的構造，強震時建築撞擊並失去隔震效益；管線可動長度不足，則在地震中拉斷，造成漏水、漏氣或火災。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Managers who do not understand the moat treat it as usable space or add structures tied to the ground during façade repairs, so the building collides and loses its isolation in a strong earthquake; utilities without enough movable length snap, causing water or gas leaks or fire. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每年沿隔震縫全周量測淨寬並拍照，檢查蓋板、伸縮踏板與管線可動接頭；地震後依檢查表記錄支承殘留變形、橡膠龜裂、鉛心外露、錨栓與刮痕板讀數，必要時抽樣更換支承並重新試驗。","textEn":"Each year measure and photograph the clear width all round the moat and inspect covers, sliding treads and flexible utility joints; after an earthquake record residual bearing offset, rubber cracking, lead exposure, anchor bolts and scratch-plate readings against a checklist, replacing and re-testing sample bearings where needed.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接文件應包含隔震設計基準、支承位置與性質表、上下限分析結果、隔震縫與可動接頭圖、檢查週期與事件後檢查表，並明訂任何在隔震縫範圍內的施作須先經結構技師核可。","textEn":"Handover should include the isolation design basis, bearing location and property tables, bound-analysis results, plans of the moat and flexible joints, inspection intervals and the post-event checklist, and state that any work within the moat zone requires prior approval by the structural engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「隔震縫維護、事件後檢查與交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Moat maintenance, post-event inspection and handover\"?","options":["每年沿隔震縫全周量測淨寬並拍照，檢查蓋板、伸縮踏板與管線可動接頭。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","隔震器只要在慢速試驗中合格，地震時的性質就一定相同。"],"optionsEn":["Each year measure and photograph the clear width all round the moat and inspect covers, sliding treads and flexible utility joints.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","If an isolator passes slow-speed tests, its properties in an earthquake will be the same."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每年沿隔震縫全周量測淨寬並拍照，檢查蓋板、伸縮踏板與管線可動接頭；地震後依檢查表記錄支承殘留變形、橡膠龜裂、鉛心外露、錨栓與刮痕板讀數，必要時抽樣更換支承並重新試驗。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Each year measure and photograph the clear width all round the moat and inspect covers, sliding treads and flexible utility joints; after an earthquake record residual bearing offset, rubber cracking, lead exposure, anchor bolts and scratch-plate readings against a checklist, replacing and re-testing sample bearings where needed. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b077-v13-40","title":"隔震縫維護、事件後檢查與交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Moat maintenance, post-event inspection and handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"prerequisiteIds":["b077-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「隔震縫淨空與管線接頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Moat clearance and utility joints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"管理單位不了解隔震縫的功能，把它當成可利用空間，或在外牆修繕時加設與地面相連的構造，強震時建築撞擊並失去隔震效益；管線可動長度不足，則在地震中拉斷，造成漏水、漏氣或火災。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Managers who do not understand the moat treat it as usable space or add structures tied to the ground during façade repairs, so the building collides and loses its isolation in a strong earthquake; utilities without enough movable length snap, causing water or gas leaks or fire. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此交接文件與日常維護必須把隔震縫當成結構構件管理，並在每次地震後檢查支承、可動接頭與隔震縫是否完整。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Handover documents and routine maintenance must therefore manage the moat as a structural element, and after every earthquake inspect bearings, flexible joints and moat clearance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「隔震改造完成後，隔震縫只是一條空隙，不需要維護。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once the retrofit is complete, the moat is just a gap that needs no maintenance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b077-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"管理單位不了解隔震縫的功能，把它當成可利用空間，或在外牆修繕時加設與地面相連的構造，強震時建築撞擊並失去隔震效益；管線可動長度不足，則在地震中拉斷，造成漏水、漏氣或火災。","textEn":"Managers who do not understand the moat treat it as usable space or add structures tied to the ground during façade repairs, so the building collides and loses its isolation in a strong earthquake; utilities without enough movable length snap, causing water or gas leaks or fire.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]},{"id":"b077-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「隔震縫維護、事件後檢查與交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Moat maintenance, post-event inspection and handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","管理單位不了解隔震縫的功能，把它當成可利用空間，或在外牆修繕時加設與地面相連的構造，強震時建築撞擊並失去隔震效益。","隔震改造會讓建築在地震中完全不動。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Managers who do not understand the moat treat it as usable space or add structures tied to the ground during façade repairs, so the building collides and loses its isolation in a strong earthquake.","Base isolation makes a building stay completely still in an earthquake."],"answer":1,"explanation":"管理單位不了解隔震縫的功能，把它當成可利用空間，或在外牆修繕時加設與地面相連的構造，強震時建築撞擊並失去隔震效益；管線可動長度不足，則在地震中拉斷，造成漏水、漏氣或火災。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Managers who do not understand the moat treat it as usable space or add structures tied to the ground during façade repairs, so the building collides and loses its isolation in a strong earthquake; utilities without enough movable length snap, causing water or gas leaks or fire. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-forell-base-isolation","v13s-forell-sf-city-hall","v13s-forell-utah-capitol","v13s-wiki-slc-county-building","v13s-ncree-bats"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
